{
 "cells": [
  {
   "kind": 1,
   "value": "# gl(3), L=2, adjoint x adjoint: the degree-<=2 transfer-matrix span and localising covectors (2026-10-10)\n\nImplements `L2-210-localising-span-spec.md`.",
   "languageId": "markdown",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 1,
   "value": "## 0. Setup\n\nPlain GT generators JJ (exact rationals), invariant metric G, everything a function of the twists. No numerics in Tasks 0-2. Q-machinery of the reference notebook is not needed (overlaps with eigenstates only need the stored transfer eigenvalues).",
   "languageId": "markdown",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 2,
   "value": "(* fresh kernel state; Quiet because the front-end wrapper symbol ClearGlobals is Protected *)\nQuiet[ClearAll[\"Global`*\"]];\n(* GT basis and gl(3) generators, verbatim from L2-rotation-sov.wb *)\nps[rep_] := ps[rep] = Block[{res = (Prepend[rep, #1] &) /@ Tuples[Table[Range[rep[[1, i + 1]], rep[[1, i]]], {i, 1, Length[rep[[1]]] - 1}]]}, If[Length[res[[1, 1]]] == 1, Reverse[Sort[res]], Reverse[Sort[Flatten[ps /@ res, 1]]]]];\ndim[rep_] := dim[rep] = Length[ps[{rep}]];\nJ0[k_][pat_] := J0[k][pat] = Sum[pat[[k, i]], {i, 1, k}] - Sum[pat[[k - 1, i]], {i, 1, k - 1}];\nJp[k_][pat_] := Jp[k][pat] = -Sum[(Product[pat[[k, i]] - i - pat[[k + 1, j]] + j, {j, Range[k + 1]}]/Product[pat[[k, i]] - i - pat[[k, j]] + j, {j, Complement[Range[k], {i}]}])*v[ReplacePart[pat, {k, i} -> pat[[k, i]] + 1]], {i, 1, k}];\nJm[k_][pat_] := Jm[k][pat] = Sum[(Product[pat[[k, i]] - i - pat[[k - 1, j]] + j, {j, Range[k - 1]}]/Product[pat[[k, i]] - i - pat[[k, j]] + j, {j, Complement[Range[k], {i}]}])*v[ReplacePart[pat, {k, i} -> pat[[k, i]] - 1]], {i, 1, k}];\nJJ[k_, l_, rep_] := JJ[k, l, rep] = Which[\n  k == l, DiagonalMatrix[J0[k] /@ ps[{rep}]],\n  l == k + 1, Transpose[Table[(Coefficient[Jp[k][ps[{rep}][[i]]], v[#1]] &) /@ ps[{rep}], {i, 1, Length[ps[{rep}]]}]],\n  l == k - 1, Transpose[Table[(Coefficient[Jm[l][ps[{rep}][[i]]], v[#1]] &) /@ ps[{rep}], {i, 1, Length[ps[{rep}]]}]],\n  l > k + 1, JJ[k, k + 1, rep] . JJ[k + 1, l, rep] - JJ[k + 1, l, rep] . JJ[k, k + 1, rep],\n  l < k - 1, JJ[k, k - 1, rep] . JJ[k - 1, l, rep] - JJ[k - 1, l, rep] . JJ[k, k - 1, rep]];\nchecks = <||>;\npr = 200; Λ = {2, 1, 0}; nL = 2; d1 = dim[Λ]; d2 = d1^nL;\nhN = 1/2; thN = {2/7, -3/5};\nEe[i_, j_] := Ee[i, j] = JJ[i, j, Λ];\nid2 = SparseArray[IdentityMatrix[d2]];\nE1[i_, j_] := E1[i, j] = SparseArray[KroneckerProduct[SparseArray[Ee[i, j]], SparseArray[IdentityMatrix[d1]]]];\nE2[i_, j_] := E2[i, j] = SparseArray[KroneckerProduct[SparseArray[IdentityMatrix[d1]], SparseArray[Ee[i, j]]]];\nwt1 = Table[Table[J0[k][p], {k, 3}], {p, ps[{Λ}]}];\nwtBasis = Flatten[Table[Table[J0[k][p1] + J0[k][p2], {k, 3}], {p1, ps[{Λ}]}, {p2, ps[{Λ}]}], 1];\ncomm = Flatten[Table[Ee[i, j] . Ee[k, l] - Ee[k, l] . Ee[i, j] - (KroneckerDelta[j, k] Ee[i, l] - KroneckerDelta[l, i] Ee[k, j]), {i, 3}, {j, 3}, {k, 3}, {l, 3}]];\nchecks[\"JJ gl(3) relations\"] = Union[comm] === {0};\n(* invariant diagonal metric G, normalized G[[1]] = 1 *)\ngv = Array[gg, d1];\ngsol = Solve[Flatten[Append[Table[Transpose[Ee[i, j]] . DiagonalMatrix[gv] - DiagonalMatrix[gv] . Ee[j, i], {i, 3}, {j, i + 1, 3}], {gv[[1]] - 1}]] == 0, gv];\ngMet = DiagonalMatrix[gv /. First[gsol]];\nchecks[\"G unique, positive, invariant for all Ee[i,j]\"] = Length[gsol] === 1 && And @@ Positive[Diagonal[gMet]] && And @@ Flatten[Table[Transpose[Ee[i, j]] . gMet === gMet . Ee[j, i], {i, 3}, {j, 3}]];\nGrid[{{\"d1, d2\", {d1, d2}}, {\"weights of the 8 site states\", ToString[wt1]}, {\"checks\", ToString[Normal[checks]]}, {\"diag G\", ToString[Diagonal[gMet]]}}, Frame -> All]",
   "languageId": "wolfram",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 2,
   "value": "(* monodromy T(v) = L1(v-th1) L2(v-th2), exact sparse. Principal minors of T.diag(z) at seven interpolation points uS; for a diagonal twist the (ix,ix) minor is (prod z_ix) times the untwisted minor, so the exact coefficient matrices tBasisC[a, ix] (of u^0..u^6) are computed once and tZexact[zz] is an exact linear combination. *)\nTm[v_] := Tm[v] = Table[Sum[(KroneckerDelta[i, k] (v - thN[[1]]) id2 + hN E1[i, k]) . (KroneckerDelta[k, j] (v - thN[[2]]) id2 + hN E2[k, j]), {k, 3}], {i, 3}, {j, 3}];\nuS = 1/7 + Range[0, 6]/3;\nminorAt[ix_, v_] := Sum[Signature[σ] Dot @@ Table[Tm[v - (k - 1) hN][[σ[[k]], ix[[k]]]], {k, Length[ix]}], {σ, Permutations[ix]}];\nvinv = Inverse[Table[uS[[k]]^j, {k, 7}, {j, 0, 6}]];\ntBasisC[a_, ix_] := tBasisC[a, ix] = With[{ms = Table[minorAt[ix, uS[[k]]], {k, 7}]}, Table[Sum[vinv[[j, k]] ms[[k]], {k, 7}], {j, 7}]];\ntZexact[zz_] := tZexact[zz] = Table[Sum[(Times @@ zz[[ix]]) tBasisC[a, ix], {ix, Subsets[Range[3], {a}]}], {a, 3}];\ntEval[tc_, a_, u0_] := Sum[u0^(j - 1) tc[[a, j]], {j, 7}];\nauditNu[hh_, ths_, n_, x_] := Product[x - ths[[s]] + hh Λ[[n]], {s, Length[ths]}];\n(* the two twist points: P1 and control P1' *)\nzP1 = {3/2, 5/4, 2/3}; wP1 = {5/2, 7/3, 3/5}; zP1c = {3/2, 5/4, 3/7}; wP1c = {7/4, -2/5, 9/7};\n{tTm, tzP1} = AbsoluteTiming[tZexact[zP1]];\n{tTm2, tzP1c} = AbsoluteTiming[tZexact[zP1c]];\nGrid[{{\"time tBasisC + tZexact(P1) (s)\", tTm}, {\"time tZexact(P1') (s)\", tTm2}, {\"coefficient matrices sparse?\", Head[tzP1[[2, 3]]]}}, Frame -> All]",
   "languageId": "wolfram",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 1,
   "value": "## Task 0. Setup checks, the coefficient operators a_1..a_6, the span D2",
   "languageId": "markdown",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 2,
   "value": "(* HW kets of V(x)V (exact; common null space of the total raising operators per weight sector), G2-orthogonal projectors (G2 = G(x)G is the invariant inner product because JJ is not Hermitian) *)\nu12raiseM = Normal[Join[E1[1, 2] + E2[1, 2], E1[1, 3] + E2[1, 3], E1[2, 3] + E2[2, 3]]];\nsecOf[mu_] := Flatten[Position[wtBasis, mu]];\nu12sectors = GatherBy[Range[d2], wtBasis[[#]] &];\nu12HW = Flatten[Table[Module[{ns = NullSpace[u12raiseM[[All, sec]]]}, Table[Normal[SparseArray[Thread[sec -> v], {d2}]], {v, ns}]], {sec, u12sectors}], 1];\nhwSecs = {{4, 2, 0}, {4, 1, 1}, {3, 3, 0}, {3, 2, 1}, {2, 2, 2}};\ngd2 = Flatten[KroneckerProduct[Diagonal[gMet], Diagonal[gMet]]];\nhwKets[mu_] := Select[u12HW, wtBasis[[FirstCase[Range[d2], k_ /; #[[k]] =!= 0]]] === mu &];\nhwH[mu_] := hwH[mu] = Transpose[hwKets[mu]];\nhwMinv[mu_] := hwMinv[mu] = Inverse[Transpose[hwH[mu]] . (gd2 hwH[mu])];\nPHWc[mu_][psi_] := hwH[mu] . (hwMinv[mu] . (Transpose[hwH[mu]] . (gd2 psi)));\nPHWall[psi_] := Sum[PHWc[mu][psi], {mu, hwSecs}];\ngNorm[psi_] := Sqrt[Total[gd2 psi^2]];\nchecks[\"number of HW kets = 6\"] = Length[u12HW];\nchecks[\"HW kets annihilated by all total raising ops\"] = And @@ (u12raiseM . # === ConstantArray[0, 3 d2] & /@ u12HW);\nchecks[\"HW multiplicities per sector (420,411,330,321,222)\"] = Length[hwKets[#]] & /@ hwSecs;\nchecks[\"sector sizes (420,411,330,321,222), total\"] = {Length[secOf[#]] & /@ hwSecs, Total[Length[secOf[#]] & /@ hwSecs]};\nchecks[\"G2-projector idempotent, fixes HW kets (exact)\"] = With[{vv = Table[(-1)^k k/7, {k, d2}]}, And @@ Table[PHWc[mu][PHWc[mu][vv]] === PHWc[mu][vv] && (And @@ (PHWc[mu][#] === # & /@ hwKets[mu])), {mu, hwSecs}]];\n(* Task 0 proper: coefficient operators a = (t1^(0), t1^(1), t2^(0..3)) and the spans D1, D2, D3 *)\nchiOf[zz_] := {Total[zz], zz[[1]] zz[[2]] + zz[[1]] zz[[3]] + zz[[2]] zz[[3]], Times @@ zz};\nzeroQ[m_] := Union[Flatten[Normal[m]]] === {0};\naOps[tc_] := {tc[[1, 1]], tc[[1, 2]], tc[[2, 1]], tc[[2, 2]], tc[[2, 3]], tc[[2, 4]]};\nd1Basis[tc_] := Join[{id2}, aOps[tc]];\nd2Basis[tc_] := Module[{a = aOps[tc]}, Join[{id2}, a, Flatten[Table[a[[i]] . a[[j]], {i, 6}, {j, i, 6}], 1]]];\nd2Names = Join[{\"1\"}, Table[\"a\" <> ToString[i], {i, 6}], Flatten[Table[\"a\" <> ToString[i] <> \"a\" <> ToString[j], {i, 6}, {j, i, 6}]]];\nd3Extra[tc_] := Module[{a = aOps[tc]}, Flatten[Table[a[[i]] . a[[j]] . a[[k]], {i, 6}, {j, i, 6}, {k, j, 6}], 2]];\nflatM[ms_] := Normal[SparseArray[Flatten /@ ms]];\n(* fused transfer matrices at a point v *)\nTfused[tc_][lam_, v_] := With[{t = Function[{a, x}, tEval[tc, a, x]]}, Switch[lam, {1, 0}, t[1, v], {1, 1}, t[2, v], {2, 0}, t[1, v] . t[1, v + hN] - t[2, v + hN], {2, 1}, t[2, v] . t[1, v + hN] - t[3, v + hN], {2, 2}, t[2, v] . t[2, v + hN] - t[3, v + hN] . t[1, v]]];\n(* determinant formula T_lam(x) = det_{ij} t_{lam'_j + i - j}(x + (i-1)h), t_0 = 1, t_<0 = 0; lam padded to length 2 *)\nTdet[tc_][lam_, x_] := Module[{lp = Table[Count[lam, l_ /; l >= j], {j, Length[lam]}], n = Length[lam], tt}, tt[m_, y_] := Which[m == 0, id2, m < 0, 0 id2, True, tEval[tc, m, y]]; Total[(Signature[#] Dot @@ Table[tt[lp[[j]] + #[[j]] - j, x + (#[[j]] - 1) hN], {j, n}]) & /@ Permutations[Range[n]]]];\ntask0[zz_] := Module[{tc = tZexact[zz], chi = chiOf[zz], a, B2, M2, rk2, v0 = thN[[1]] - 2 hN, res = <||>, memb, rel},\n  a = aOps[tc];\n  res[\"t1 coefficient u^2 = chi1 id, u^3..u^6 = 0\"] = zeroQ[tc[[1, 3]] - chi[[1]] id2] && And @@ (zeroQ /@ tc[[1, 4 ;; 7]]);\n  res[\"t2 coefficient u^4 = chi2 id, u^5,u^6 = 0\"] = zeroQ[tc[[2, 5]] - chi[[2]] id2] && And @@ (zeroQ /@ tc[[2, 6 ;; 7]]);\n  res[\"t3(u) = chi3 nu1 nu2 nu3 id at u = 1/5, -3/7\"] = And @@ Table[zeroQ[tEval[tc, 3, u0] - chi[[3]] auditNu[hN, thN, 1, u0] auditNu[hN, thN, 2, u0 - hN] auditNu[hN, thN, 3, u0 - 2 hN] id2], {u0, {1/5, -3/7}}];\n  res[\"all 15 pairs [a_i,a_j] = 0 and [t1(1/5),t2(2/3)] = 0\"] = (And @@ Flatten[Table[zeroQ[a[[i]] . a[[j]] - a[[j]] . a[[i]]], {i, 6}, {j, i + 1, 6}]]) && zeroQ[tEval[tc, 1, 1/5] . tEval[tc, 2, 2/3] - tEval[tc, 2, 2/3] . tEval[tc, 1, 1/5]];\n  B2 = d2Basis[tc]; M2 = flatM[B2]; rk2 = MatrixRank[M2];\n  res[\"rank D1 (7 expected), rank D2 (28 expected)\"] = {MatrixRank[flatM[d1Basis[tc]]], rk2};\n  rel = NullSpace[Transpose[M2]];\n  res[\"number of linear relations among the 28 basis operators; rank of each relation's support\"] = {Length[rel], Length /@ (Select[#, # =!= 0 &] & /@ rel)};\n  res[\"rank of D2 + cubic monomials (64 = everything expected)\"] = MatrixRank[Join[M2, flatM[d3Extra[tc]]]];\n  memb[Tm_] := MatrixRank[Join[M2, {Flatten[Normal[Tm]]}]] == rk2;\n  res[\"T11(th1-2h), T21(th1-2h) in D2\"] = {memb[Tfused[tc][{1, 1}, v0]], memb[Tfused[tc][{2, 1}, v0]]};\n  res[\"all T_lam(th1-2h) and T_lam(th2+h), lam <= (2,2), in D2\"] = And @@ Flatten[Table[memb[Tfused[tc][lam, v]], {lam, {{1, 0}, {1, 1}, {2, 0}, {2, 1}, {2, 2}}}, {v, {v0, thN[[2]] + hN}}]];\n  res[\"T_lam = determinant formula for lam = (2,0),(2,1),(2,2) at x = 1/3\"] = {zeroQ[Tfused[tc][{2, 0}, 1/3] - Tdet[tc][{2, 0}, 1/3]], zeroQ[Tfused[tc][{2, 1}, 1/3] - Tdet[tc][{2, 1}, 1/3]], zeroQ[Tfused[tc][{2, 2}, 1/3] - Tdet[tc][{2, 2}, 1/3]]};\n  res];\n{tT0a, t0P1} = AbsoluteTiming[task0[zP1]];\nt0P1c = task0[zP1c];\nGrid[Join[{{\"Task 0 at P1 (time s)\", tT0a}}, Normal[t0P1], {{\"same at P1' identical?\", t0P1 === t0P1c}}, {{\"HW/metric checks\", ToString[Normal[checks]]}}], Frame -> All, Alignment -> Left]",
   "languageId": "wolfram",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 1,
   "value": "**Task 0 result (printed output of the cell above; VS Code does not execute cells of this file, so each cell was evaluated in the shared kernel via the saved cell source and the output is recorded here).**\n\n- gl(3) relations, invariant metric G (diag 1,1,1,2,6,9,4,9): pass. 6 HW kets (multiplicities 420:1, 411:1, 330:1, 321:2, 222:1), sector sizes (1,2,2,6,10) total 21; projector check pass.\n- t1 u^2 coefficient = chi1 id and u^3..u^6 = 0; t2 u^4 coefficient = chi2 id and u^5,u^6 = 0; t3(u) = chi3 nu1 nu2 nu3 id at two points; all 15 [a_i,a_j] = 0 and [t1,t2] = 0 exactly: all True (P1 and P1').\n- **rank D1 = 7; rank D2 = 24, not 28.** There are 4 independent linear relations among the 28 operators {1, a_i, a_i a_j} (supports of size 13, 12, 14, 13 monomials; identical count at P1 and P1'): they are four quadratic relations among the a_i (the 64 joint eigenvalue tuples lie on a proper subvariety). Cubic span D2 + {a_i a_j a_k} has rank **48, not 64** (same at P1' and P1), so the cubic level is not vacuous: the commutative algebra is 64-dim only at higher degree.\n- T11(th1-2h), T21(th1-2h) in D2: True, True. All five fused shapes T_lam at th1-2h and th2+h lie in D2: True. Fused shapes agree with the determinant formula (lam = (2,0),(2,1),(2,2)): True (the fix of the first draft of this check, which compared (2,0) against the (1,1) determinant, is included).\n- time 1.8 s for both points.",
   "languageId": "markdown",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 1,
   "value": "## Task 1. The localising subspaces L1, L2 (exact)",
   "languageId": "markdown",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 2,
   "value": "(* exact helpers: nilpotent exponentials, torus rho(diag) (0^0 = 1 handled), one-site vacuum rotation Omega_{(w1,w2,w3)} (w3 drops out), one-site twisted transfer matrices *)\nzs = {z[1], z[2], z[3]}; ws = {w[1], w[2], w[3]};\nexpN[a_] := IdentityMatrix[Length[a]] + a + a . a/2 + a . a . a/6 + a . a . a . a/24;\nchecks[\"expN = MatrixExp on root generators (exact)\"] = And @@ Flatten[Table[If[i == j, True, expN[c Ee[i, j]] === MatrixExp[c Ee[i, j]]], {i, 3}, {j, 3}, {c, {3/7, -5/2, 2}}]];\nρdiag[d_] := DiagonalMatrix[Table[Product[If[J0[k][p] === 0, 1, d[[k]]^J0[k][p]], {k, 3}], {p, ps[{Λ}]}]];\noneSiteVac[zz_, ww_] := Module[{rOmx}, rOmx = {r1 -> (w[1] - z[1])/(w[1] - z[2]), r2 -> ((w[1] - z[1]) (-w[2] + z[1]) (z[2] - z[3]))/((z[1] - z[2]) (w[1] - z[3]) (w[2] - z[3])), r3 -> ((w[1] - z[2]) (-w[2] + z[2]) (z[1] - z[3]))/((z[1] - z[2]) (w[1] - z[3]) (-w[2] + z[3]))} /. Join[Thread[zs -> zz], Thread[ws -> ww]];\n  First[{UnitVector[d1, 1]} . expN[(r1 /. rOmx) Ee[1, 2]] . expN[(r2 /. rOmx) Ee[1, 3]] . expN[(r3 /. rOmx) Ee[2, 3]]]];\nLone[i_, j_, v_] := KroneckerDelta[i, j] (v - thN[[1]]) IdentityMatrix[d1] + hN Ee[i, j];\n(* one-site (site 1 only) twisted principal-minor transfer matrix t_a(v) *)\ntOne[zz_][a_, v_] := Sum[(Times @@ zz[[ix]]) Sum[Signature[σ] Dot @@ Table[Lone[σ[[k]], ix[[k]], v - (k - 1) hN], {k, Length[ix]}], {σ, Permutations[ix]}], {ix, Subsets[Range[3], {a}]}];\nT11one[zz_] := tOne[zz][2, thN[[1]] - 2 hN];\nT21one[zz_] := tOne[zz][2, thN[[1]] - 2 hN] . tOne[zz][1, thN[[1]] - hN] - tOne[zz][3, thN[[1]] - hN];\nwtIdx = Table[Flatten[Position[wt1, m]], {m, Union[wt1]}]; wtList = Union[wt1];\nGrid[{{\"expN check\", checks[\"expN = MatrixExp on root generators (exact)\"]}, {\"weights (sorted)\", ToString[wtList]}, {\"dims\", ToString[Length /@ wtIdx]}, {\"vac(P1) first entries\", ToString[oneSiteVac[zP1, wP1][[1 ;; 3]]]}}, Frame -> All]",
   "languageId": "wolfram",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 2,
   "value": "(* localising data: Phi_X = <Om x Om|X reshaped 8x8 (row = site 1, column = site 2). Phi_X = v (x) Om iff Phi_X . n = 0 for all kets n annihilated by Om. Unknown coefficients c over a basis of D2 (or D1); exact NullSpace. *)\nlocData[zz_, om_, basisFn_ : d2Basis] := Module[{tc = tZexact[zz], B, nB, Om2, phis, ann, k0, A1, A2, s1, s2, v1s, u2s, L1b, L2b, rowsOf},\n  B = basisFn[tc]; nB = Length[B]; Om2 = Flatten[KroneckerProduct[om, om]];\n  phis = Table[Partition[Normal[Om2 . b], d1], {b, B}];\n  ann = NullSpace[{om}]; k0 = UnitVector[d1, FirstCase[Range[d1], k_ /; om[[k]] =!= 0]];\n  A1 = Transpose[Table[Flatten[phis[[k]] . Transpose[ann]], {k, nB}]];\n  A2 = Transpose[Table[Flatten[ann . phis[[k]]], {k, nB}]];\n  s1 = NullSpace[A1]; s2 = NullSpace[A2];\n  v1s = Table[((c . phis) . k0)/(om . k0), {c, s1}]; u2s = Table[(k0 . (c . phis))/(om . k0), {c, s2}];\n  rowsOf[m_] := If[m === {}, {}, DeleteCases[RowReduce[m], {0 ..}]];\n  <|\"nB\" -> nB, \"phis\" -> phis, \"A\" -> Transpose[Flatten /@ phis], \"om\" -> om, \"tc\" -> tc, \"B\" -> B, \"dimSol1\" -> Length[s1], \"dimSol2\" -> Length[s2], \"L1\" -> rowsOf[v1s], \"L2\" -> rowsOf[u2s], \"sol1\" -> s1, \"sol2\" -> s2,\n   \"kernel\" -> nB - MatrixRank[Flatten /@ phis], \"rankPhi\" -> MatrixRank /@ phis, \"colSpace\" -> MatrixRank[Join @@ phis], \"rowSpace\" -> MatrixRank[Join @@ (Transpose /@ phis)]|>];\ncovRank[m_] := If[m === {}, 0, MatrixRank[m]];\ncoverage[L_] := Table[covRank[L[[All, ix]]], {ix, wtIdx}];\nrep1[zz_, ww_] := Module[{om = oneSiteVac[zz, ww], dd, d1d, tc, ctrl, T11v, T21v, res = <||>},\n  dd = locData[zz, om]; d1d = locData[zz, om, d1Basis];\n  res[\"l1, l2 (D2)\"] = {Length[dd[\"L1\"]], Length[dd[\"L2\"]]};\n  res[\"dim of coefficient solution spaces (site1, site2)\"] = {dd[\"dimSol1\"], dd[\"dimSol2\"]};\n  res[\"l1, l2 (D1 only)\"] = {Length[d1d[\"L1\"]], Length[d1d[\"L2\"]]};\n  res[\"kernel dim {X in D2 : <Om Om|X = 0}, rank of the map X -> <OmOm|X\"] = {dd[\"kernel\"], dd[\"nB\"] - dd[\"kernel\"]};\n  res[\"weights\"] = wtList;\n  res[\"L1 weight coverage (rank of projected L1 per weight)\"] = coverage[dd[\"L1\"]];\n  res[\"L2 weight coverage\"] = coverage[dd[\"L2\"]];\n  T11v = om . T11one[zz]; T21v = om . T21one[zz];\n  res[\"controls: Om1, Om1 T11one, Om1 T21one in L1 (D2)\"] = (covRank[Append[dd[\"L1\"], #]] == Length[dd[\"L1\"]]) & /@ {om, T11v, T21v};\n  res[\"controls rank of {Om1, Om1 T11one, Om1 T21one}, equals l1?\"] = {MatrixRank[{om, T11v, T21v}], MatrixRank[{om, T11v, T21v}] == Length[dd[\"L1\"]]};\n  res[\"L1(D1) contains the three controls\"] = (covRank[Append[d1d[\"L1\"], #]] == Length[d1d[\"L1\"]]) & /@ {om, T11v, T21v};\n  res[\"rank of Phi_X for each of the 28 basis ops\"] = dd[\"rankPhi\"];\n  res[\"joint site-2 column space dim, site-1 row space dim (of all Phi_X)\"] = {dd[\"colSpace\"], dd[\"rowSpace\"]};\n  (* the actual L=2 fused operators: <Om Om|T11(th1-2h) = s (Om T11one) (x) Om ? *)\n  res[\"<OmOm|T11(th1-2h) vs (Om T11one)(x)Om, <OmOm|T21(th1-2h) vs (Om T21one)(x)Om: rank of each pair (1 = proportional)\"] = With[{tcz = dd[\"tc\"], Om2 = Flatten[KroneckerProduct[om, om]], v0 = thN[[1]] - 2 hN}, {MatrixRank[{Flatten[Partition[Om2 . Tfused[tcz][{1, 1}, v0], d1]], Flatten[Outer[Times, T11v, om]]}], MatrixRank[{Flatten[Partition[Om2 . Tfused[tcz][{2, 1}, v0], d1]], Flatten[Outer[Times, T21v, om]]}]}];\n  res];\n{tL1a, rP1} = AbsoluteTiming[rep1[zP1, wP1]];\nGrid[Join[{{\"time P1 (s)\", tL1a}}, Normal[rP1]], Frame -> All, Alignment -> Left]",
   "languageId": "wolfram",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 1,
   "value": "**Task 1 result (P1: z = (3/2,5/4,2/3), w = (5/2,7/3,3/5); P1' gives the identical table).** (Cell 9 setup: expN check True; weights (0,1,2),(0,2,1),(1,0,2),(1,1,1),(1,2,0),(2,0,1),(2,1,0), dims 1,1,1,2,1,1,1.)\n\n- **l1 = 3, l2 = 3** (D2). Coefficient solution space has dim 7 = 4 (kernel of X -> <OmOm|X, which is exactly the four operator relations) + 3. D1 only: l1 = l2 = 2.\n- Weight coverage of L1 (rank of the projection onto each weight, in the order above): (1,1,1,2,1,1,1) -- every weight is hit and (1,1,1) with rank 2, but L1 is only 3-dimensional, NOT 8.\n- Controls: Om1, Om1 T11one, Om1 T21one all in L1; they have rank 3 so they span L1 exactly. In D1 only the first two are in L1 (Om1 T21one needs a quadratic term). The L=2 operators T11(th1-2h), T21(th1-2h) give <OmOm|T = s (Om T_one)(x)Om with proportional site-1 factors (rank-1 pairs): True, True.\n- Rank of Phi_X for the 28 basis operators: 1,3,2,3,3,3,2,6,5,8,8,8,6,3,6,6,6,4,7,7,7,6,7,7,6,7,6,3. Joint site-2 column space of all Phi_X: 8, site-1 row space: 8 (both full).\n- time 0.14 s per point.",
   "languageId": "markdown",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 1,
   "value": "## Task 2. Targets (exact)",
   "languageId": "markdown",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 2,
   "value": "(* membership v in L1 and the canonical coefficients of a representative: the unique solution supported on the pivot columns of the 64 x 28 map c -> Phi(c); all other basis operators (the kernel directions, 4 of them) set to zero. Linear in v, so polynomial dependence of v on a parameter carries over to c. *)\nmemb1[dd_, v_] := covRank[Append[dd[\"L1\"], v]] == Length[dd[\"L1\"]];\npivOf[A_] := Module[{rr = DeleteCases[RowReduce[A], {0 ..}]}, Table[LengthWhile[row, # === 0 &] + 1, {row, rr}]];\ncoefOf[dd_, v_] := Module[{A = dd[\"A\"], piv, b = Flatten[Outer[Times, v, dd[\"om\"]]], cp, c = ConstantArray[0, dd[\"nB\"]]}, piv = pivOf[A]; cp = Quiet[LinearSolve[A[[All, piv]], b]];\n  If[Head[cp] === LinearSolve || A[[All, piv]] . cp =!= b, $Failed, c[[piv]] = cp; c]];\nnzC[c_] := If[c === $Failed, \"not in\", With[{pos = Select[Range[Length[c]], c[[#]] =!= 0 &]}, Thread[d2Names[[pos]] -> c[[pos]]]]];\nw2ps = {3/7, -11/5, 9/4, 7/3, 13/10};\nth12 = thN[[1]] - thN[[2]]; t12 = th12/hN; y0 = (th12 - hN)/(th12 - 2 hN);\ntargets[zz_, ww_] := Module[{om = oneSiteVac[zz, ww], dd, res = <||>, cA, w1 = ww[[1]], w2 = ww[[2]], ystar, omS, ddS, vS, wOther, polyU, s},\n  dd = locData[zz, om];\n  (* (a) polynomial torus *)\n  cA = Table[With[{v = om . ρdiag[w2p - zz]}, {memb1[dd, v], coefOf[dd, v]}], {w2p, w2ps}];\n  res[\"(a) membership, w2' = 3/7, -11/5, 9/4, 7/3, 13/10\"] = cA[[All, 1]];\n  vS = om . ρdiag[s - zz]; polyU = Table[Coefficient[vS, s, j], {j, 0, 3}];\n  res[\"(a) polynomial coefficient vectors u_j (w2'^j), j = 0..3: each in L1?  rank{L1,u_0..u_3}, rank{u_0..u_3}\"] = {(memb1[dd, #] & /@ polyU), covRank[Join[dd[\"L1\"], polyU]], covRank[polyU]};\n  res[\"(a) u_3 = Om1 (id), u_0 = -Om1 rho(z)\"] = {polyU[[4]] === om, polyU[[1]] === -(om . ρdiag[zz])};\n  res[\"(b) Om1 rho(z), Om1 rho(1/z)\"] = {memb1[dd, om . ρdiag[zz]], memb1[dd, om . ρdiag[1/zz]]};\n  res[\"(c) resolvent Om1 rho(1/(w2'-z)), w2' = -11/5, 9/4\"] = {memb1[dd, om . ρdiag[1/(-11/5 - zz)]], memb1[dd, om . ρdiag[1/(9/4 - zz)]]};\n  wOther = If[ww === wP1, wP1c, wP1];\n  res[\"(d) second vacuum Om(z,w'), Om(z,{w1,3,1}), Om(z,{w1,-1/2,1})\"] = {memb1[dd, oneSiteVac[zz, wOther]], memb1[dd, oneSiteVac[zz, {w1, 3, 1}]], memb1[dd, oneSiteVac[zz, {w1, -1/2, 1}]]};\n  (* (e) the product point of Two-rotations-det-overlap section 5: base vacuum with second parameter y = y0 w2 *)\n  ystar = y0 w2; omS = oneSiteVac[zz, {w1, ystar, 1}]; ddS = locData[zz, omS];\n  res[\"(e) y* = y0 w2; l1, l2 of the base Om*; Om* rho(1/(w2-z)) in L1(Om*)?; Om* in L1(Om*)?\"] = {ystar, {Length[ddS[\"L1\"]], Length[ddS[\"L2\"]]}, memb1[ddS, omS . ρdiag[1/(w2 - zz)]], memb1[ddS, omS]};\n  <|\"res\" -> res, \"cA\" -> cA, \"dd\" -> dd, \"polyU\" -> polyU|>];\n{tT2, tgP1} = AbsoluteTiming[targets[zP1, wP1]];\ntgP1c = targets[zP1c, wP1c];\nGrid[Join[{{\"time P1 (s)\", tT2}, {\"y0, t12\", {y0, t12}}}, Normal[tgP1[\"res\"]], {{\"P1' (control)\", \"\"}}, Normal[tgP1c[\"res\"]]], Frame -> All, Alignment -> Left]",
   "languageId": "wolfram",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 2,
   "value": "(* (e) regression, correct reading: base vacuum Om_w on both sites, target <Om_w x Om_w|X = v (x) Om_ystar with v = Om_ystar rho(1/(w2-z)), Om_ystar = oneSiteVac[z, {w1, y0 w2, 1}]. The site-2 factor is the OTHER rotation, so this is a statement about the image of D2, not about L1 of the base vacuum. *)\nprodPoint[zz_, ww_] := Module[{om = oneSiteVac[zz, ww], dd, ystar = y0 ww[[2]], omS, v, b, A, rA, rAb, piv, cp},\n  dd = locData[zz, om]; omS = oneSiteVac[zz, {ww[[1]], ystar, 1}]; v = omS . ρdiag[1/(ww[[2]] - zz)]; b = Flatten[Outer[Times, v, omS]]; A = dd[\"A\"]; piv = pivOf[A];\n  rA = MatrixRank[A]; rAb = MatrixRank[Join[A, Transpose[{b}], 2]];\n  cp = If[rA == rAb, Quiet[LinearSolve[A[[All, piv]], b]], $Failed];\n  <|\"ystar\" -> ystar, \"rank A, rank [A|b]\" -> {rA, rAb}, \"rank{Om_w, Om_ystar} (site-2 factor differs from base)\" -> MatrixRank[{om, omS}], \"coefficients (pivot rep)\" -> If[cp === $Failed, \"not in\", Select[Thread[d2Names[[piv]] -> cp], #[[2]] =!= 0 &]], \"v\" -> v, \"om2\" -> omS, \"cvec\" -> If[cp === $Failed, $Failed, Normal[SparseArray[Thread[piv -> cp], 28]]]|>];\nprP1 = prodPoint[zP1, wP1]; prP1c = prodPoint[zP1c, wP1c];\n(* sum-of-products diagnostics: M = X in D2 whose site-2 row space of Phi_X lies inside span of Om1 and om2, om2 = Om(z,{w1,z2,1}) (r3 = 0 rotation) *)\nsumProd[zz_, ww_] := Module[{om = oneSiteVac[zz, ww], dd, w1 = ww[[1]], om2, ann2, A2, sM, phiM, vv, vvp, rowsOf, rotChk, rs, vA, vS, polyU, s, dec},\n  dd = locData[zz, om]; om2 = oneSiteVac[zz, {w1, zz[[2]], 1}];\n  rs = {(w1 - zz[[1]])/(w1 - zz[[2]]), ((w1 - zz[[1]]) (-zz[[2]] + zz[[1]]) (zz[[2]] - zz[[3]]))/((zz[[1]] - zz[[2]]) (w1 - zz[[3]]) (zz[[2]] - zz[[3]]))};\n  rotChk = om2 === UnitVector[d1, 1] . expN[rs[[1]] Ee[1, 2]] . expN[rs[[2]] Ee[1, 3]];\n  ann2 = NullSpace[{om, om2}];\n  A2 = Transpose[Table[Flatten[dd[\"phis\"][[k]] . Transpose[ann2]], {k, dd[\"nB\"]}]];\n  sM = NullSpace[A2]; phiM = Table[c . dd[\"phis\"], {c, sM}];\n  rowsOf[m_] := If[m === {}, {}, DeleteCases[RowReduce[m], {0 ..}]];\n  (* Phi = v (x) om + v' (x) om2, row by row *)\n  dec = Table[Transpose[Table[LinearSolve[Transpose[{om, om2}], ph[[i]]], {i, d1}]], {ph, phiM}];\n  vv = dec[[All, 1]]; vvp = dec[[All, 2]];\n  vA = rowsOf[vv];\n  vS = om . ρdiag[s - zz]; polyU = Table[Coefficient[vS, s, j], {j, 0, 3}];\n  <|\"om2 is rotation e1 exp(r1 E12) exp(r2 E13), r3 = 0\" -> rotChk, \"rank{om, om2}\" -> MatrixRank[{om, om2}], \"dim of coefficient solution space\" -> Length[sM], \"dim M mod kernel (rank of Phi images)\" -> MatrixRank[Flatten /@ phiM], \"dim span of site-1 factors v (Om1 part)\" -> Length[vA], \"dim span of v' (om2 part)\" -> covRank[vvp], \"dim span{v, v'} jointly\" -> covRank[Join[vv, vvp]],\n   \"weights covered by span of v\" -> coverage[vA], \"u_j (torus polynomial coeffs) in span of v: \" -> (covRank[Append[vA, #]] == Length[vA] & /@ polyU), \"Om1 rho(1/z) in span v\" -> (covRank[Append[vA, om . ρdiag[1/zz]]] == Length[vA]), \"rank {span v, u_0..u_3}\" -> covRank[Join[vA, polyU]]|>];\nGrid[Join[{{\"(e) corrected regression P1\", \"\"}}, Normal[KeyDrop[prP1, {\"v\", \"om2\", \"cvec\"}]], {{\"(e) P1'\", \"\"}}, Normal[KeyDrop[prP1c, {\"v\", \"om2\", \"cvec\"}]]], Frame -> All, Alignment -> Left]",
   "languageId": "wolfram",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 2,
   "value": "{tSP, spP1} = AbsoluteTiming[sumProd[zP1, wP1]]; spP1c = sumProd[zP1c, wP1c];\nGrid[Join[{{\"sum of products P1 (time s)\", tSP}}, Normal[spP1], {{\"P1'\", \"\"}}, Normal[spP1c]], Frame -> All, Alignment -> Left]",
   "languageId": "wolfram",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 1,
   "value": "**Task 2 result (cell 13 targets, cell 14 corrected (e) and sum-of-products, cell 15 prints).** See the table in the final markdown cell; summary of what the exact runs gave, identical at P1 and P1':\n\n- (a) polynomial torus Om1 rho(diag(w2'-z)): NOT in L1 for any of the five w2' (False x5). Coefficient vectors u_j of w2'^j: u_3 = Om1 (in L1), u_0 = -Om1 rho(z) (NOT in L1), u_1, u_2 not in L1; rank{L1, u_0..u_3} = 6 = 3 + 3.\n- (b) Om1 rho(z): NOT in L1; **Om1 rho(1/z): in L1** (a surprise; the two are different torus translates).\n- (c) resolvent Om1 rho(1/(w2'-z)), w2' = -11/5, 9/4: not in L1 (as expected).\n- (d) second vacuum Om(z,w') and Om(z,{w1,y,1}), y = 3, -1/2: not in L1.\n- (e) literal reading of the spec (base = Om_{(w1,y*)} on both sites): Om* rho(1/(w2-z)) not in L1(Om*) (False), l1 = l2 = 3 for that base. The meaningful regression (cell 14) is with base Om_w and target v (x) Om_{(w1,y*)} where the site-2 factor is the other rotation: **in the image of D2 at both points** (rank A = rank [A|b] = 24), so the method reproduces the known product point; rank{Om_w, Om_{(w1,y*)}} = 2 (the factors differ).\n- Sum of products M (site-2 row space in span{Om1, om2}, om2 = Om(z,{w1,z2,1}) is the r3 = 0 rotation, checked): dim M mod kernel = 5, span of the Om1-side site-1 factors has dim 5 covering all weights (1,1,1,2,1,1,1), span of the om2-side factors has dim 2, jointly 6. u_0, u_1, u_2 of the polynomial torus are still NOT in the span; Om1 rho(1/z) is; rank{span v, u_0..u_3} = 8 (they generate everything).",
   "languageId": "markdown",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 1,
   "value": "### Exploratory (beyond the spec): do the cubic and quartic spans reach the torus translate?\n\nTask 0 found rank D2 = 24 and rank(D2 + cubic) = 48, not 28/64, so the higher levels are not vacuous. Same localising scan with the cubic span D3 and the quartic span D4.",
   "languageId": "markdown",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 2,
   "value": "d3Basis[tc_] := Join[d2Basis[tc], d3Extra[tc]];\nd4Extra[tc_] := Module[{a = aOps[tc]}, Flatten[Table[a[[i]] . a[[j]] . a[[k]] . a[[l]], {i, 6}, {j, i, 6}, {k, j, 6}, {l, k, 6}], 3]];\nd4Basis[tc_] := Join[d3Basis[tc], d4Extra[tc]];\n(* pick an independent subset of the monomials once per level so that locData works with a basis of the true span (kernel-free) *)\nindepBasis[fn_][tc_] := Module[{B = fn[tc], M, piv}, M = flatM[B]; piv = pivOf[Transpose[M]]; B[[piv]]];\nlevelScan[zz_, ww_, fn_] := Module[{om = oneSiteVac[zz, ww], dd, vS, polyU, s, res = <||>},\n  dd = locData[zz, om, indepBasis[fn]];\n  vS = om . ρdiag[s - zz]; polyU = Table[Coefficient[vS, s, j], {j, 0, 3}];\n  <|\"dim of span\" -> dd[\"nB\"], \"l1, l2\" -> {Length[dd[\"L1\"]], Length[dd[\"L2\"]]}, \"image rank\" -> dd[\"nB\"] - dd[\"kernel\"], \"L1 coverage\" -> coverage[dd[\"L1\"]],\n   \"(a) w2' = 3/7,-11/5,9/4,7/3,13/10\" -> (memb1[dd, om . ρdiag[# - zz]] & /@ w2ps), \"u_0..u_3 in L1\" -> (memb1[dd, #] & /@ polyU), \"(b) rho(z), rho(1/z)\" -> {memb1[dd, om . ρdiag[zz]], memb1[dd, om . ρdiag[1/zz]]},\n   \"(c) resolvent -11/5, 9/4\" -> {memb1[dd, om . ρdiag[1/(-11/5 - zz)]], memb1[dd, om . ρdiag[1/(9/4 - zz)]]}, \"(d) 2nd vacuum, y = 3, -1/2\" -> {memb1[dd, oneSiteVac[zz, If[ww === wP1, wP1c, wP1]]], memb1[dd, oneSiteVac[zz, {ww[[1]], 3, 1}]], memb1[dd, oneSiteVac[zz, {ww[[1]], -1/2, 1}]]}|>];\n{tD3, lsD3} = AbsoluteTiming[levelScan[zP1, wP1, d3Basis]];\n{tD4, lsD4} = AbsoluteTiming[levelScan[zP1, wP1, d4Basis]];\nGrid[Join[{{\"D3 (time s)\", tD3}}, Normal[lsD3], {{\"D4 (time s)\", tD4}}, Normal[lsD4]], Frame -> All, Alignment -> Left]",
   "languageId": "wolfram",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 1,
   "value": "**Exploratory result (cell 18, P1).** Cubic span D3 (84 monomials, independent rank 48, 0.8 s): l1 = l2 = 3, same coverage, (a) False x5, u_0..u_2 not in L1, (b) rho(z) False / rho(1/z) True, (c), (d) all False: the cubic level adds nothing for the localising question. Quartic span D4 (210 monomials, independent rank 64 = all of End on the 64-dim space, 3.0 s): l1 = l2 = 8, everything in L1 (vacuous: the commutative algebra is 64-dim from degree 4). So the first level where the torus translate becomes a Q-number is degree 4 in the six coefficients a_i, where it is a statement about the full 64-dim algebra and the 'bounded number of brackets' argument does not hold (a quartic has up to 210 monomials).",
   "languageId": "markdown",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 1,
   "value": "## Task 2'. Q-number check on the chain (numeric, pr = 200, exact twist P1)",
   "languageId": "markdown",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 2,
   "value": "(* the 21 eigenstates of the five HW sectors at the exact twist (numeric, precision pr), with the eigenvalues alpha_i of the six coefficient operators a_i read off at the largest component *)\nstatesAt[zz_] := Module[{tz = tZexact[zz], tn, aN, out = {}},\n  tn = Table[N[Normal[tz[[a, j]]], pr], {a, 3}, {j, 7}];\n  aN = {tn[[1, 1]], tn[[1, 2]], tn[[2, 1]], tn[[2, 2]], tn[[2, 3]], tn[[2, 4]]};\n  Do[Module[{sec = secOf[mu], mix, es},\n    mix = (Sum[(3/7)^(j - 1) tn[[1, j]], {j, 7}] + N[Pi, pr] Sum[(3/7)^(j - 1) tn[[2, j]], {j, 7}])[[sec, sec]];\n    es = Eigensystem[mix];\n    Do[Module[{psiS = es[[2, k]], psi, km, al},\n      km = First@Ordering[Abs[psiS], -1]; psiS = psiS/psiS[[km]];\n      psi = Normal[SparseArray[Thread[sec -> psiS], {d2}]];\n      al = Table[(aN[[i]] . psi)[[sec[[km]]]]/psi[[sec[[km]]]], {i, 6}];\n      AppendTo[out, <|\"mu\" -> mu, \"psi\" -> psi, \"al\" -> al, \"res\" -> Max[Table[Norm[aN[[i]] . psi - al[[i]] psi]/Norm[psi], {i, 6}]]|>]], {k, Length[sec]}]], {mu, hwSecs}];\n  out];\nXB[c_, al_] := c[[1]] + c[[2 ;; 7]] . al + c[[8 ;; 28]] . Flatten[Table[al[[i]] al[[j]], {i, 6}, {j, i, 6}]];\n(* relative deviation of <phi|Psi_B> from X^B <Om x Om|Psi_B> over all states *)\nqDev[sts_, cvec_, phi_, Om2_] := Max[Table[With[{lhs = phi . s[\"psi\"], rhs = XB[cvec, s[\"al\"]] (Om2 . s[\"psi\"])}, Abs[lhs - rhs]/Max[Abs[lhs], Abs[rhs], 10^-100]], {s, sts}]];\n{tSt, stsP1} = AbsoluteTiming[statesAt[zP1]];\nddP1 = locData[zP1, oneSiteVac[zP1, wP1]];\nomP1 = oneSiteVac[zP1, wP1]; Om2P1 = Flatten[KroneckerProduct[omP1, omP1]];\n(* representative of target (b): Om1 rho(1/z) *)\nvB = omP1 . ρdiag[1/zP1]; cB = coefOf[ddP1, vB];\ndevB = qDev[stsP1, cB, Flatten[Outer[Times, vB, omP1]], Om2P1];\n(* representative of the product point (e): v (x) Om_ystar *)\ndevE = qDev[stsP1, prP1[\"cvec\"], Flatten[Outer[Times, prP1[\"v\"], prP1[\"om2\"]]], Om2P1];\n(* control with a wrong coefficient vector: perturb one coefficient *)\ndevCtl = qDev[stsP1, cB + UnitVector[28, 5] 10^-3, Flatten[Outer[Times, vB, omP1]], Om2P1];\nGrid[{{\"time states (s)\", tSt}, {\"# states, sector counts\", {Length[stsP1], Length[Select[stsP1, #[\"mu\"] === {3, 2, 1} &]]}}, {\"max eigen-residual of the a_i\", ScientificForm[Max[stsP1[[All, \"res\"]]], 3]}, {\"Precision of psi\", Min[Precision /@ stsP1[[All, \"psi\"]]]}, {\"(b) Om1 rho(1/z): representative (nonzero coefficients)\", ToString[nzC[cB]]}, {\"(b) number of nonzero c\", Count[cB, _?(# =!= 0 &)]}, {\"(b) max rel deviation <v(x)Om1|Psi> vs X^B <OmOm|Psi>\", ScientificForm[devB, 3]}, {\"(e) product point: number of nonzero c, max rel deviation\", {Count[prP1[\"cvec\"], _?(# =!= 0 &)], ScientificForm[devE, 3]}}, {\"control: wrong coefficient (+1e-3 on a_3)\", ScientificForm[devCtl, 3]}}, Frame -> All, Alignment -> Left]",
   "languageId": "wolfram",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 1,
   "value": "**Task 2' result (cell 21).** 21 states of the five HW sectors at the exact twist P1 (pr = 200, 0.14 s); the six a_i have simultaneous eigenvectors with residual 0 (accuracy 196 digits). Best targets: (b) Om1 rho(1/z) [representative with 15 nonzero c out of 28, kernel directions set to zero] and the corrected (e) product point [18 nonzero c]. Max relative deviation of <v (x) Om|Psi_B> from X^B <Om (x) Om|Psi_B>, X^B = c_0 + sum c_i alpha_i + sum_{i<=j} c_ij alpha_i alpha_j: **(b) < 1e-194 (printed 0 at accuracy 194), (e) < 1e-194 (0 at accuracy 194)**, while the control with one coefficient shifted by 1e-3 gives 3.5e-3, so the check is sensitive.\n\nStatement: for every X in D2 the overlap <v (x) Om1|Psi_B> equals det6(w) times a polynomial of degree 2 in the six eigenvalue coefficients alpha^B = (t1^(0), t1^(1), t2^(0..3)) (each a Wronskian/Cramer expression in the dual Q's, not re-derived here), with at most 1 + 6 + 21 = 28 terms (24 independent) for any representation at L = 2.",
   "languageId": "markdown",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
