  {
   "kind": 1,
   "value": "## Task 4. Cost statement\n\nFor ANY representation at L = 2 the covector <Om (x) Om|X, X in D2, needs only the six transfer-matrix eigenvalue coefficients alpha = (t1^(0), t1^(1), t2^(0), t2^(1), t2^(2), t2^(3)) (t1 at 2 points, t2 at 4 points; t1^(2) = chi1, t2^(4) = chi2, t3 = qdet are known scalars) plus the overlap <Om (x) Om|Psi_B> = det6; the degrees of t_a(u) depend only on L and gl(N). The representatives found have 15 (target (b) Om1 rho(1/z)) and 18 (product point (e)) nonzero coefficients out of the 24 independent operators (4 of the 28 monomials are linearly dependent; the kernel directions were set to zero). Caveat found here: D2 has dimension 24 (not 28), the cubic span 48, the quartic span 64; the torus translate with polynomial dependence (a) is not reached before degree 4. Follow-ups (not in this notebook): [3,1,0] with the same rank scan; gl(4) [S,S,0,0] at S = 2 with D2 of t1..t4 (expect again fewer than the naive count of monomials and a possible mismatch between the localising span and the torus family).",
   "languageId": "markdown",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 1,
   "value": "### gl(3) adj⊗adj localising-span result (2026-10-10)\n\nExecution note: VS Code did not execute cells of this new file (runCell returns NOT executed); every code cell was evaluated in the shared kernel K1 by reading its saved source (`ToExpression` of the cell value) and the printed results are recorded in the markdown cells under each code cell. The code cells therefore have no native outputs.\n\n| item | P1 | P1' |\n|---|---|---|\n| rank D1 / D2 / D3 / D4 | 7 / 24 / 48 / 64 | same |\n| relations among the 28 monomials of D2 | 4 | 4 |\n| l1, l2 (D2) | 3, 3 | 3, 3 |\n| l1, l2 (D1) | 2, 2 | 2, 2 |\n| l1 (D3, rank 48) | 3 | (P1 only) |\n| l1 (D4) | 8 | (P1 only) |\n| L1 coverage per weight (0,1,2),(0,2,1),(1,0,2),(1,1,1),(1,2,0),(2,0,1),(2,1,0) | 1,1,1,2,1,1,1 | same |\n| L1 = span{Om1, Om1 T11one, Om1 T21one} | yes | yes |\n| (a) polynomial torus, 5 values of w2' | all NOT in L1 | all NOT in L1 |\n| (b) Om1 rho(z) / Om1 rho(1/z) | no / **yes** (= -(128/75) Om1 T21one) | no / yes (-(25088/6075)) |\n| (c) resolvent, 2 values | no, no | no, no |\n| (d) second vacuum, y = 3, y = -1/2 | no, no, no | no, no, no |\n| (e) literal reading (base Om_{(w1,y*)}) | Om* rho in L1(Om*): no; l1 = 3 | no |\n| (e) corrected (base Om_w, v (x) Om_{(w1,y*)}) | in image of D2, 18 nonzero c | in image |\n| sum of products M (om2 = Om(z,{w1,z2,1})) | dim 5, v-span 5, v'-span 2, joint 6; torus u_0,u_1,u_2 not in span | same |\n| Task 2' deviation | (b) and (e) both < 1e-194 (control 3.5e-3) | not run |\n| Task 3 | not run (stop rule) | |\n\nStructural surprises: (1) rank D2 = 24 and cubic rank 48 (not 28, 64): there are four quadratic relations among the a_i; the full algebra is only reached at degree 4. (2) l1 = 3 only; the polynomial torus translate (a) is not a Q-number of degree <= 3, so the gl(4)-style double localising deformation is not available from the transfer-matrix span here. (3) The spec's literal target (e) is not in L1; the product point is a statement about the site-2 factor being a different rotation. (4) Om1 rho(1/z) is in L1 (it is proportional to Om1 T21one).",
