  {
   "kind": 2,
   "value": "(* independent bases (7 for D1, 24 for D2) and their pivot positions inside the monomial list d2Names (28 entries) *)\nindepPiv[fn_][tc_] := pivOf[Transpose[flatM[fn[tc]]]];\nbasisOf[tc_, k_] := If[k == 1, d1Basis[tc][[indepPiv[d1Basis][tc]]], d2Basis[tc][[indepPiv[d2Basis][tc]]]];\npivK[tc_, k_] := If[k == 1, indepPiv[d1Basis][tc], indepPiv[d2Basis][tc]];\n(* solve Phi . Q = Om2 . P over P in BP, Q in BQ; ns rows are (p coefficients, q coefficients). dimQ0 = dimension of the P = 0 solutions (Phi . Q = 0 only) *)\nt5solve[Om2_, Phi_, BP_, BQ_] := Module[{M, ns, pz, nP = Length[BP]},\n  M = Transpose[Join[Table[-(Om2 . Normal[b]), {b, BP}], Table[Phi . Normal[b], {b, BQ}]]];\n  ns = NullSpace[M]; pz = NullSpace[Transpose[Table[Phi . Normal[b], {b, BQ}]]];\n  <|\"ns\" -> ns, \"dim\" -> Length[ns], \"dimQ0\" -> Length[pz], \"dimEff\" -> Length[ns] - Length[pz], \"nP\" -> nP|>];\nrandVec = With[{}, SeedRandom[7]; Table[RandomInteger[{-5, 5}]/RandomInteger[{1, 5}], {8}]];\ntgts[zz_, ww_] := Module[{om = oneSiteVac[zz, ww], w1 = ww[[1]], om2, wd, cL},\n  om2 = oneSiteVac[zz, {w1, zz[[2]], 1}]; wd = If[ww === wP1, wP1c, wP1];\n  cL = If[MemberQ[zz, 3/7], {13/10, 9/4}, {3/7, 9/4}];\n  Join[\n   Table[\"(a) w2'=\" <> ToString[x] -> Flatten[Outer[Times, om . ρdiag[x - zz], om]], {x, {3/7, -11/5, 9/4}}],\n   Table[\"(c) w2'=\" <> ToString[x] -> Flatten[Outer[Times, om . ρdiag[1/(x - zz)], om]], {x, cL}],\n   {\"(d) Om_w'\" -> Flatten[Outer[Times, oneSiteVac[zz, wd], om]], \"(d) y=3\" -> Flatten[Outer[Times, oneSiteVac[zz, {w1, 3, 1}], om]], \"(d) y=-1/2\" -> Flatten[Outer[Times, oneSiteVac[zz, {w1, -1/2, 1}], om]]},\n   Table[\"(f) site2 kappa=\" <> ToString[k] -> Flatten[Outer[Times, om, om + k om2]], {k, {1, -2}}],\n   Table[\"(f) site1 kappa=\" <> ToString[k] -> Flatten[Outer[Times, om + k om2, om]], {k, {1, -2}}],\n   {\"(g) Om1 rho(1/z)\" -> Flatten[Outer[Times, om . ρdiag[1/zz], om]], \"(g) random v\" -> Flatten[Outer[Times, randVec, om]]}]];\ntask5table[zz_, ww_] := Module[{tc = tZexact[zz], om = oneSiteVac[zz, ww], Om2, tg = tgts[zz, ww]},\n  Om2 = Flatten[KroneckerProduct[om, om]];\n  Table[t[[1]] -> Table[With[{r = t5solve[Om2, t[[2]], basisOf[tc, pq[[1]]], basisOf[tc, pq[[2]]]]}, {r[\"dim\"], r[\"dimQ0\"], r[\"dimEff\"]}], {pq, {{1, 1}, {1, 2}, {2, 1}, {2, 2}}}], {t, tg}]];\n{tT5, t5P1} = AbsoluteTiming[task5table[zP1, wP1]];\nt5P1c = task5table[zP1c, wP1c];\nGrid[Join[{{\"time P1 (s)\", tT5}, {\"entries: {dim, dim(P=0), dim effective} for (P,Q) = (D1,D1),(D1,D2),(D2,D1),(D2,D2)\", \"\"}, {\"P1\", \"\"}}, Table[{t[[1]], ToString[t[[2]]]}, {t, t5P1}], {{\"P1'\", \"\"}}, Table[{t[[1]], ToString[t[[2]]]}, {t, t5P1c}]], Frame -> All, Alignment -> Left]",
   "languageId": "wolfram",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 1,
   "value": "**Task 5 scan result (cell 29, 11 s for both points, identical at P1 and P1').** Entries are {dim of solution space, dim with P = 0, effective dim}. Zero everywhere (all four slot pairs (D1,D1),(D1,D2),(D2,D1),(D2,D2)) for: (a) w2' = 3/7, -11/5, 9/4; (c) resolvent (w2' = 3/7, 9/4 at P1; 13/10, 9/4 at P1' since 3/7 = z3 there); (d) Om_w' (the other vacuum); (g) random v.\n\nNonzero only in the slot pair (P,Q) = (D2,D2) unless stated: (d) Om_{(w1,y,1)}, y = 3 and y = -1/2: dimension 6 each; (f) site-2 line Om1 (x) (Om1 + kappa om2), kappa = 1, -2: dimension 5 each; (f) site-1 line (Om1 + kappa om2) (x) Om1: dimension 6 each; (g) control Om1 rho(1/z): dimensions 1 (D1,D1), 4 (D1,D2), 4 (D2,D1), 11 (D2,D2). No P = 0 solutions anywhere (effective dim = dim). Random v: 0 as required.",
   "languageId": "markdown",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 2,
   "value": "(* for the solved targets: representative (P,Q) in (D2,D2) = generic combination of the solution space; counts, exact det of Q (64 x 64), Q^B and P^B on the 21 HW-sector states, chain identity Phi.Psi Q^B = P^B <Om Om|Psi>, and how many distinct X^B = P^B/Q^B functions the solution space contains (rank over the 21 states) *)\nevOf[al_] := Join[{1}, al, Flatten[Table[al[[i]] al[[j]], {i, 6}, {j, i, 6}]]];\nt5rep[zz_, ww_, Phi_, sts_] := Module[{tc = tZexact[zz], om = oneSiteVac[zz, ww], Om2, BP, BQ, pv, r, ns, gen, p, q, Qm, detQ, pivs, qB, pB, dev, xs},\n  Om2 = Flatten[KroneckerProduct[om, om]]; BP = basisOf[tc, 2]; BQ = basisOf[tc, 2]; pivs = pivK[tc, 2];\n  r = t5solve[Om2, Phi, BP, BQ]; ns = r[\"ns\"]; If[ns === {}, Return[\"no solution\"]];\n  gen = Table[k, {k, Length[ns]}] . ns; p = gen[[1 ;; 24]]; q = gen[[25 ;; 48]];\n  Qm = q . (Normal /@ BQ); detQ = Det[Qm];\n  qB = Table[evOf[s[\"al\"]][[pivs]] . q, {s, sts}]; pB = Table[evOf[s[\"al\"]][[pivs]] . p, {s, sts}];\n  dev = Max[Table[Abs[(Phi . sts[[i]][\"psi\"]) qB[[i]] - pB[[i]] (Om2 . sts[[i]][\"psi\"])]/Max[Abs[(Phi . sts[[i]][\"psi\"]) qB[[i]]], Abs[pB[[i]] (Om2 . sts[[i]][\"psi\"])], 10^-100], {i, Length[sts]}]];\n  xs = Table[With[{pp = v[[1 ;; 24]], qq = v[[25 ;; 48]]}, Table[(evOf[s[\"al\"]][[pivs]] . pp)/(evOf[s[\"al\"]][[pivs]] . qq), {s, sts}]], {v, ns}];\n  <|\"dim\" -> Length[ns], \"nonzero c in P, in Q\" -> {Count[p, _?(# =!= 0 &)], Count[q, _?(# =!= 0 &)]}, \"det Q exact nonzero\" -> (detQ =!= 0), \"min |Q^B| over 21 states\" -> N[Min[Abs[qB]], 5], \"max |Q^B|\" -> N[Max[Abs[qB]], 5], \"chain rel dev\" -> N[dev, 5], \"rank of X^B functions of the solution space (21 states)\" -> If[Min[Abs[qB]] == 0, \"Q^B=0 somewhere\", MatrixRank[N[xs, 60]]], \"rank of Q-parts alone (exact)\" -> MatrixRank[ns[[All, 25 ;; 48]]]|>];\nstsP1c = statesAt[zP1c];\nrepTgts[zz_, ww_, sts_] := Module[{tg = tgts[zz, ww]}, Table[t[[1]] -> t5rep[zz, ww, t[[2]], sts], {t, Select[tg, ! StringStartsQ[#[[1]], \"(a)\"] && ! StringStartsQ[#[[1]], \"(c)\"] && # =!= tg[[6]] && ! StringContainsQ[#[[1]], \"random\"] &]}]];\n{tR, repP1} = AbsoluteTiming[repTgts[zP1, wP1, stsP1]];\nrepP1c = repTgts[zP1c, wP1c, stsP1c];\nGrid[Join[{{\"time P1 (s)\", tR}}, Flatten[Table[{{t[[1]], \"\"}, Sequence @@ If[AssociationQ[t[[2]]], Normal[t[[2]]], {{\"result\", t[[2]]}}]}, {t, repP1}], 1], {{\"P1'\", \"\"}}, Flatten[Table[{{t[[1]], \"\"}, Sequence @@ If[AssociationQ[t[[2]]], Normal[t[[2]]], {{\"result\", t[[2]]}}]}, {t, repP1c}], 1]], Frame -> All, Alignment -> Left]",
   "languageId": "wolfram",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 1,
   "value": "**Task 5 representative / chain result (cell 31; 3.5 s at P1, same at P1').** Representative (P,Q) in (D2,D2) = generic combination (coefficients 1..dim) of the solution space; all solved targets have 24 nonzero c in P and 24 in Q (all 24 independent operators used).\n\n| target | solution dim | det Q (exact 64x64) | min / max abs Q^B over 21 states, P1 | same at P1' (min / max) | chain rel dev | rank of the X^B = P^B/Q^B functions in the solution space |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| (d) Om_{(w1,3,1)} | 6 | nonzero | 1.38 / 26.9 | 91.9 / 257.8 | < 1e-193 | 1 |\n| (d) Om_{(w1,-1/2,1)} | 6 | nonzero | 1.38 / 26.9 | 91.9 / 257.8 | < 1e-193 | 1 |\n| (f) site 2: Om1 (x) (Om1 + kappa om2), kappa = 1 and -2 | 5 | nonzero | 67.6 / 815.0 | 111.6 / 304.8 | < 1e-193 | 1 |\n| (f) site 1: (Om1 + kappa om2) (x) Om1, kappa = 1 and -2 | 6 | nonzero | 1.38 / 26.9 | 91.9 / 257.8 | < 1e-192 | 1 |\n| (g) Om1 rho(1/z) | 11 | nonzero | 9.42 / 244.99 | 6.86 / 256.3 | < 1e-193 | 1 |\n\nSo the chain identity <v (x) Om1|Psi_B> Q^B = P^B <Om (x) Om|Psi_B> holds to better than 1e-192 on all 21 states, Q^B is nowhere zero, Q is exactly invertible, and the ratio X^B = P^B/Q^B is unique for each target (all solutions in the space give the same function on the 21 states; only the Q-part has freedom: rank of the Q parts alone = the solution dimension). Identical numbers of Q^B for (d) y = 3, y = -1/2 and the site-1 kappa lines show they share the same 6-dim Q space.\n\n**Solvers:** (d) second-parameter vacuum Om_{(w1,y,1)} (any y tested), and the omega2 line (f), in (D2,D2) only (not in the smaller pairs); NOT solvable: (a) polynomial torus, (c) resolvent, (d) the genuinely different vacuum Om_{w'}, random v. By the spec's priority, Task 3 is run for the family (d) with v1 = Om_{(w1,y,1)}, v2 = Om_w, y = 1 + eps*eta as the free second parameter (the k of the old family), X^B = P^B/Q^B.",
   "languageId": "markdown",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 1,
   "value": "## Task 3 for the family (d): v2 = Om_w, v1 = Om_{(w1,y,1)}, regime z = 1+eps phi, w = (1+eps om1, 1+eps om2, 1+eps 5/13), y = 1+eps eta\n\n(i) Exact eps-structure of the undone covector phi_u = v1 rho(n)^-1 (n = Gauss matrix of v2 with second parameter w2): symbolic eps.",
   "languageId": "markdown",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
