  {
   "kind": 2,
   "value": "(* undo machinery: v2 = oneSiteVac[z,{w1,w2,1}] = e1^T rho(n), n from u12rs with second parameter w2 *)\nu12e1 = UnitVector[d1, 1];\nu12rs[zz_, w1_, y_] := {(w1 - zz[[1]])/(w1 - zz[[2]]), ((w1 - zz[[1]]) (zz[[1]] - y) (zz[[2]] - zz[[3]]))/((zz[[1]] - zz[[2]]) (w1 - zz[[3]]) (y - zz[[3]])), ((w1 - zz[[2]]) (zz[[2]] - y) (zz[[1]] - zz[[3]]))/((zz[[1]] - zz[[2]]) (w1 - zz[[3]]) (zz[[3]] - y))};\nu12nMat[zz_, w1_, y_] := With[{rv = u12rs[zz, w1, y]}, {{1, rv[[1]], rv[[2]] + rv[[1]] rv[[3]]}, {0, 1, rv[[3]]}, {0, 0, 1}}];\nu12rN[zz_, w1_, y_] := With[{rv = u12rs[zz, w1, y]}, expN[rv[[1]] Ee[1, 2]] . expN[rv[[2]] Ee[1, 3]] . expN[rv[[3]] Ee[2, 3]]];\nu12rNinv[zz_, w1_, y_] := With[{rv = u12rs[zz, w1, y]}, expN[-rv[[3]] Ee[2, 3]] . expN[-rv[[2]] Ee[1, 3]] . expN[-rv[[1]] Ee[1, 2]]];\nregF[eps_, ph_, om1_, om2_, eta_] := <|\"eps\" -> eps, \"z\" -> 1 + eps ph, \"w1\" -> 1 + eps om1, \"w2\" -> 1 + eps om2, \"y\" -> 1 + eps eta, \"w\" -> {1 + eps om1, 1 + eps om2, 1 + eps 5/13}|>;\nv2Of[R_] := oneSiteVac[R[\"z\"], {R[\"w1\"], R[\"w2\"], 1}];\nv1Of[R_] := oneSiteVac[R[\"z\"], {R[\"w1\"], R[\"y\"], 1}];\nphiOf[R_] := v1Of[R] . u12rNinv[R[\"z\"], R[\"w1\"], R[\"w2\"]];\ncheckUndo = With[{R = regF[10^-6, {1/3, -2/7, 5/11}, 3/4, -1/5, 7/2]}, v2Of[R] === u12e1 . u12rN[R[\"z\"], R[\"w1\"], R[\"w2\"]]];\nepsS = Symbol[\"epsS\"];\nom1s = {3/4, -5/3}; om2s = {-1/5, 9/7, 5/3}; etas = {-12/5, 7/2, 1/8};\nomGrid = Flatten[Table[{o1, o2, e}, {o1, om1s}, {o2, om2s}, {e, etas}], 2];\nphiP = {1/3, -2/7, 5/11}; phiC = {-2/5, 3/8, 7/11};\nser[expr_, k_] := Table[SeriesCoefficient[expr, {epsS, 0, j}], {j, 0, k}];\nphiSer[ph_, o1_, o2_, e_, nmax_] := Module[{R = regF[epsS, ph, o1, o2, e]}, ser[#, nmax] & /@ (Together /@ phiOf[R])];\nleadOrd[c_] := If[AllTrue[c, # === 0 &], 99, LengthWhile[c, # === 0 &]];\n{tS1, s1pt} = AbsoluteTiming[phiSer[phiP, 3/4, -1/5, 7/2, 6]];\nGrid[{{\"undo exact (v2 = e1 rho(n))\", checkUndo}, {\"grid points\", Length[omGrid]}, {\"time one point (s)\", tS1}, {\"lead orders of the 8 components (one point)\", ToString[leadOrd /@ s1pt]}}, Frame -> All]",
   "languageId": "wolfram",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 2,
   "value": "(* (i) the 18-point grid for phi and phi', symbolic eps: per site-1 weight lead order and rank of the eps^0 coefficient vectors; first the exact algebraic reason for the zeros: v1 rho(n)^-1 = e1 rho(n(y) n(w2)^-1) and the (1,2) entry of n(y) n(w2)^-1 is r1 - r1 = 0 because r1 depends on w1 only *)\nwtOfComp = wt1;\nrankTabF[ph_] := Module[{ser18 = Table[phiSer[ph, o[[1]], o[[2]], o[[3]], 3], {o, omGrid}]},\n  Table[With[{ix = wtIdx[[m]]}, With[{c0 = Table[s[[ix, 1]], {s, ser18}], c1 = Table[s[[ix, 2]], {s, ser18}]}, {wtList[[m]], Length[ix], MatrixRank[c0], MatrixRank[c1], Union[Flatten[Table[leadOrd[s[[i]]], {s, ser18}, {i, ix}]]]}]], {m, Length[wtList]}]];\n{tRkF, rkF1} = AbsoluteTiming[rankTabF[phiP]];\nrkF2 = rankTabF[phiC];\n(* which state indices carry the nonzero components, and their weights *)\nnzComps = Flatten[Position[phiSer[phiP, 3/4, -1/5, 7/2, 3][[All, 1]], _?(# =!= 0 &), {1}, Heads -> False]];\nGrid[Join[{{\"weight\", \"dim\", \"rank eps^0\", \"rank eps^1\", \"lead orders over grid (99 = zero through eps^3)\"}}, rkF1, {{\"phi' control\", \"\", \"\", \"\", \"\"}}, rkF2, {{\"time (s)\", tRkF}, {\"state indices and weights of the nonzero phi components\", ToString[{nzComps, wt1[[nzComps]]}]}, {\"identical tables\", rkF1 === rkF2}}], Frame -> All, Alignment -> Left]",
   "languageId": "wolfram",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 1,
   "value": "**3(i) result (cells 34-35; identical for phi and phi', time 0.3 s).** The undone covector phi_u = v1 rho(n)^-1 = e1 rho(n(y) n(w2)^-1) has the (1,2) entry of n(y) n(w2)^-1 equal to r1 - r1 = 0 (r1 depends on w1 only), so only TWO of the eight site-1 weights are nonzero, **exactly for all eps (zero through eps^3 on all 18 grid points, and identically by the algebra)**: weights (2,1,0) and (2,0,1) (state indices 1, 2), both O(1) with rank 1; the weights (0,1,2),(0,2,1),(1,0,2),(1,1,1),(1,2,0) are identically zero. So the second-parameter family does not untwist the E12 direction (w1 is common to both vacua), and it can only see the HW branches [4,2,0] and [4,1,1]; for [3,3,0], both octets and the singlet S = 0 exactly and R_C = K.",
   "languageId": "markdown",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 2,
   "value": "(* chain side (ii)-(iii) for the family: lean branches (HW-limit branches only), Gauss factors of the physical frame and the SoV vacuum x0 with the factorized inverse (verbatim from the reference) *)\nrsSol = {s[1] -> z[1]^2/((z[1] - z[2]) (z[1] - z[3])), s[2] -> -(z[2]/(z[1] (z[2] - z[3]))), s[3] -> 1/(z[1] z[2]), r[1] -> -(z[3]/z[2]), r[2] -> -(z[3]/z[1]), r[3] -> (z[2]^2 (-z[1] + z[3]))/(z[1]^2 (z[2] - z[3]))};\nx0Of[zz_] := Module[{rs, ppinv, pminv, dinv, x},\n  rs = rsSol /. Thread[zs -> zz];\n  ppinv = expN[-((zz[[1]] + zz[[2]])/(zz[[1]] zz[[2]])) Ee[2, 3]] . expN[(1/(zz[[1]] zz[[2]])) Ee[1, 3]] . expN[-(1/zz[[1]]) Ee[1, 2]];\n  pminv = expN[-(r[3] /. rs) Ee[2, 1]] . expN[-(r[2] /. rs) Ee[3, 1]] . expN[-(r[1] /. rs) Ee[3, 2]];\n  dinv = DiagonalMatrix[Table[Product[(s[k] /. rs)^(-J0[k][p]), {k, 3}], {p, ps[{Λ}]}]];\n  x = UnitVector[d1, 1] . ppinv . dinv . pminv; Flatten[KroneckerProduct[x, x]]];\nhwList = {{{4, 2, 0}, 1}, {{4, 1, 1}, 1}, {{3, 3, 0}, 1}, {{3, 2, 1}, 1}, {{3, 2, 1}, 2}, {{2, 2, 2}, 1}};\nbranchesLean[zz_] := Module[{zn = N[zz, pr], tz, tn, x0, out = {}},\n  tz = tZexact[zz]; tn = Table[N[Normal[tz[[a, j]]], pr], {a, 3}, {j, 7}]; x0 = x0Of[zn];\n  Do[Module[{sec = secOf[mu], mix, es, rr, nHW = Length[hwKets[mu]], pick, raise},\n    mix = (Sum[(3/7)^(j - 1) tn[[1, j]], {j, 7}] + N[Pi, pr] Sum[(3/7)^(j - 1) tn[[2, j]], {j, 7}])[[sec, sec]];\n    es = Eigensystem[mix]; raise = N[Normal[Join[E1[1, 2] + E2[1, 2], E1[2, 3] + E2[2, 3]]][[All, sec]], pr];\n    rr = Table[Norm[raise . v]/Norm[v], {v, es[[2]]}]; pick = SortBy[Ordering[rr, nHW], Re[es[[1, #]]] &];\n    Do[Module[{psiS = es[[2, pick[[c]]]]}, psiS = psiS/(x0[[sec]] . psiS); AppendTo[out, <|\"mu\" -> mu, \"copy\" -> c, \"psi\" -> Normal[SparseArray[Thread[sec -> psiS], {d2}]], \"rr\" -> rr[[pick[[c]]]]|>]], {c, nHW}]], {mu, hwSecs}];\n  out];\nchainRun[phv_, epsv_] := Module[{zz = regF[epsv, phv, 0, 0, 0][\"z\"], br, brs, hws},\n  br = branchesLean[zz]; brs = Table[First@Select[br, #[\"mu\"] === h[[1]] && #[\"copy\"] === h[[2]] &], {h, hwList}];\n  hws = PHWall /@ brs[[All, \"psi\"]];\n  <|\"rr\" -> brs[[All, \"rr\"]], \"hw\" -> hws, \"pts\" -> Table[With[{R = regF[epsv, phv, o[[1]], o[[2]], o[[3]]]}, With[{v1 = N[v1Of[R], pr], v2 = N[v2Of[R], pr], phN = N[phiOf[R], pr]}, With[{phi2 = Flatten[KroneckerProduct[v1, v2]], phiu = Flatten[KroneckerProduct[phN, u12e1]]}, Table[{phi2 . brs[[b]][\"psi\"], phi2 . hws[[b]], phiu . hws[[b]] v2[[1]]}, {b, 6}]]]], {o, omGrid}]|>];\n{tCh, chP1} = AbsoluteTiming[chainRun[phiP, 10^-6]];\nGrid[{{\"time one (phi, eps) run (s)\", tCh}, {\"raising residual rr of the 6 branches\", ToString[N[chP1[\"rr\"], 3]]}, {\"max undo deviation |S - s <phi (x) e1|P_HW Psi>| / |S| (4,1,1), (4,2,0)\", ToString[N[Table[Max[Table[Abs[chP1[\"pts\"][[g, b, 2]] - chP1[\"pts\"][[g, b, 3]]]/Max[Abs[chP1[\"pts\"][[g, b, 2]]], 10^-300], {g, 18}]], {b, {1, 2}}], 3]]}, {\"max |S| for branches 3..6 (should be 0)\", ToString[N[Table[Max[Abs[chP1[\"pts\"][[All, b, 2]]]], {b, 3, 6}], 3]]}}, Frame -> All]",
   "languageId": "wolfram",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 1,
   "value": "**Chain cell 37 result (phi, eps = 1e-6; 0.6 s).** Undo exact: max |S - s<phi (x) e1|P_HW Psi>|/|S| < 1e-184 for [4,2,0] and [4,1,1]. S = 0 to absolute 1e-122 or below for [3,3,0], both octets, the singlet, as predicted by the two-weight support. rr of the HW-limit branches ~ 2e-7.",
   "languageId": "markdown",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 2,
   "value": "epsList = {10^-6, 2 10^-6, 4 10^-6};\nrunsF = Table[ph -> Table[chainRun[ph, e], {e, epsList}], {ph, {phiP, phiC}}];\nmedAt[r_, b_, k_] := Median[Abs[r[\"pts\"][[All, b, k]]]];\nexpo[f_] := N[{Log2[f[2]/f[1]], Log2[f[3]/f[2]]}, 4];\nstatsF[ph_, runs_] := Table[With[{Sf = Function[ei, medAt[runs[[ei]], b, 2]], Rf = Function[ei, medAt[runs[[ei]], b, 1]], Kf = Function[ei, Median[Abs[runs[[ei]][\"pts\"][[All, b, 1]] - runs[[ei]][\"pts\"][[All, b, 2]]]]]},\n  {hwList[[b]], \"S exps\" -> If[Sf[1] < 10^-100, \"S = 0\", expo[Sf]], \"K exps\" -> expo[Kf], \"max|K/S| at eps 1,2,4e-6\" -> If[Sf[1] < 10^-100, \"undefined\", N[Table[Max[Abs[(runs[[ei]][\"pts\"][[All, b, 1]] - runs[[ei]][\"pts\"][[All, b, 2]])/runs[[ei]][\"pts\"][[All, b, 2]]]], {ei, 3}], 3]]}], {b, 6}];\nstP = statsF[phiP, runsF[[1, 2]]]; stC = statsF[phiC, runsF[[2, 2]]];\n(* (iii) CG of [4,1,1] from the overlap alone: slice state 2 (weight (2,0,1)) times e1; chain slice = <m_2 (x) e1|P_HW Psi> = hw[[9]] *)\ncgF[ph_, runs_] := Module[{ph20 = Table[phiSer[ph, o[[1]], o[[2]], o[[3]], 0][[2, 1]], {o, omGrid}], res},\n  res = Table[With[{r = runs[[ei]]}, With[{cq = Table[r[\"pts\"][[g, 2, 1]]/ph20[[g]], {g, 18}], cc = r[\"hw\"][[2, 9]]}, {N[Max[Abs[cq/cc - 1]], 4], cc, cq}]], {ei, 3}];\n  rich[f_] := (8 f[[1]] - 6 f[[2]] + f[[3]])/3;\n  <|\"phi2(0) over grid (min,max)\" -> N[{Min[ph20], Max[ph20]}, 5], \"max rel err |C_Q/C_chain - 1| at eps 1,2,4e-6\" -> res[[All, 1]], \"chain slice * eps^3 at the three eps\" -> N[Table[res[[ei, 2]] epsList[[ei]]^3, {ei, 3}], 12], \"Richardson limit chain\" -> N[rich[Table[res[[ei, 2]] epsList[[ei]]^3, {ei, 3}]], 12], \"Richardson limit C_Q, grid point 1 and 18\" -> N[{rich[Table[res[[ei, 3, 1]] epsList[[ei]]^3, {ei, 3}]], rich[Table[res[[ei, 3, 18]] epsList[[ei]]^3, {ei, 3}]]}, 12]|>];\ncgP = cgF[phiP, runsF[[1, 2]]]; cgC = cgF[phiC, runsF[[2, 2]]];\nGrid[Join[{{\"phi primary: per branch\", \"\"}}, Table[{ToString[t[[1]]], ToString[Rest[t]]}, {t, stP}], {{\"phi' control\", \"\"}}, Table[{ToString[t[[1]]], ToString[Rest[t]]}, {t, stC}], {{\"[4,1,1] CG, phi\", \"\"}}, Normal[cgP], {{\"[4,1,1] CG, phi'\", \"\"}}, Normal[cgC]], Frame -> All, Alignment -> Left]",
   "languageId": "wolfram",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 1,
   "value": "**3(ii)/(iii) result (cell 39; runs for phi and phi', eps = 1,2,4 e-6, 18 grid points each).**\n\n| branch | S exps (eps 1->2, 2->4) | K exps | max abs K/S at eps = 1,2,4 e-6 (phi) | same (phi') |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| [4,2,0] | -2, -2 | K = 0 exactly | 0 | 0 |\n| [4,1,1] | -3, -3 | -2, -2 | 1.11e-6, 2.22e-6, 4.43e-6 | 7.3e-7, 1.46e-6, 2.91e-6 |\n| [3,3,0] | S = 0 exactly | -2 | undefined | undefined |\n| octet 1 | S = 0 | -3 | undefined | undefined |\n| octet 2 | S = 0 | -3 | undefined | undefined |\n| singlet | S = 0 | -4 | undefined | undefined |\n\nSo K/S = O(eps) for the two visible branches, but the other four branches have S = 0 and R_C = K entirely: this family reads no information about [3,3,0], the octets or the singlet.\n\n[4,1,1] CG from the overlap alone (slice weight (2,0,1), C_Q = R_C / phi2(0), phi2(0) in (-0.943, 2.153) over the grid for phi; (-4.03, 1.78) for phi'): max relative error over the 18 grid points |C_Q/C_chain - 1| = 1.108e-6, 2.216e-6, 4.433e-6 at eps = 1,2,4e-6 (phi), 7.28e-7, 1.456e-6, 2.911e-6 (phi'), i.e. linear in eps. Richardson limits of eps^3 times the chain slice: **46.67453891138 (phi)**, matching the reference [4,1,1] value 46.67453891 at P1; and -12.35023562230 (phi'). Richardson limit of eps^3 C_Q at grid points 1 and 18 agrees with the chain limit to all 12 digits printed. No octet mixing or [3,3,0]/singlet CG can be extracted.",
   "languageId": "markdown",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 2,
   "value": "(* 3(iv): exact (P,Q) at the regime point: v1 (x) v2 as the target, base v2 (x) v2; solution space and a canonical representative (reduced row echelon basis of the solution space, combination with coefficients 1..dim); chain check R_C = P^B/Q^B <v2 (x) v2|Psi_B> on the 6 branches; eps-exponents of all 48 coefficients over eps = 1,2,4e-6 *)\niv[ph_, e_, g_] := Module[{o = omGrid[[g]], R, zz, tc, v1, v2, Phi, Om2, BP, r, ns, gen, brs, tn, aN, pivs, devs, pq},\n  R = regF[e, ph, o[[1]], o[[2]], o[[3]]]; zz = R[\"z\"]; tc = tZexact[zz]; v2 = v2Of[R]; v1 = v1Of[R];\n  Phi = Flatten[Outer[Times, v1, v2]]; Om2 = Flatten[Outer[Times, v2, v2]]; BP = basisOf[tc, 2];\n  r = t5solve[Om2, Phi, BP, BP]; ns = RowReduce[r[\"ns\"]]; gen = Table[k, {k, Length[ns]}] . ns; pivs = pivK[tc, 2];\n  brs = Table[First@Select[branchesLean[zz], #[\"mu\"] === h[[1]] && #[\"copy\"] === h[[2]] &], {h, hwList}];\n  tn = Table[N[Normal[tc[[a, j]]], pr], {a, 3}, {j, 7}]; aN = {tn[[1, 1]], tn[[1, 2]], tn[[2, 1]], tn[[2, 2]], tn[[2, 3]], tn[[2, 4]]};\n  devs = Table[Module[{psi = b[\"psi\"], km, al, mv, pB, qB, lhs, rhs},\n    km = First@Ordering[Abs[psi], -1]; al = Table[(aN[[i]] . psi)[[km]]/psi[[km]], {i, 6}]; mv = evOf[al][[pivs]];\n    pB = mv . gen[[1 ;; 24]]; qB = mv . gen[[25 ;; 48]];\n    lhs = N[Phi, pr] . psi; rhs = pB/qB (N[Om2, pr] . psi); {Abs[lhs - rhs]/Abs[lhs], Abs[qB]}], {b, brs}];\n  <|\"dim\" -> r[\"dim\"], \"gen\" -> gen, \"devs\" -> devs|>];\nivRuns = Table[iv[phiP, e, 1], {e, epsList}];\nexpC = Table[N[Log2[Abs[ivRuns[[k + 1, \"gen\"]]/ivRuns[[k, \"gen\"]]]], 4], {k, 2}];\nGrid[{{\"solution-space dimension at eps = 1,2,4e-6\", ToString[ivRuns[[All, \"dim\"]]]}, {\"chain check max rel dev |<v1 (x) v2|Psi> - P^B/Q^B <v2 (x) v2|Psi>|/|.|, 6 branches, eps=1e-6, 2e-6, 4e-6\", ToString[N[Table[Max[r[\"devs\"][[All, 1]]], {r, ivRuns}], 3]]}, {\"min |Q^B| over the 6 branches\", ToString[N[Table[Min[r[\"devs\"][[All, 2]]], {r, ivRuns}], 3]]}, {\"eps-exponents of the 48 coefficients (P then Q), eps 1->2: min, max\", ToString[{Min[expC[[1]]], Max[expC[[1]]]}]}, {\"eps 2->4: min, max\", ToString[{Min[expC[[2]]], Max[expC[[2]]]}]}, {\"distinct rounded exponents 1->2\", ToString[Union[Round[expC[[1]]]]]}, {\"distinct rounded exponents 2->4\", ToString[Union[Round[expC[[2]]]]]}, {\"nonzero coefficients (P,Q)\", ToString[{Count[ivRuns[[1, \"gen\"]][[1 ;; 24]], _?(# =!= 0 &)], Count[ivRuns[[1, \"gen\"]][[25 ;; 48]], _?(# =!= 0 &)]}]}}, Frame -> All, Alignment -> Left]",
   "languageId": "wolfram",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 1,
   "value": "**3(iv) result (cell 41, P-grid point 1, phi, eps = 1,2,4e-6).** Exact (P,Q) in (D2,D2) for the target v1 (x) v2 over the base v2 (x) v2 at the regime point: solution-space dimension 6 at all three eps (same as at finite twist); both P and Q have 24 nonzero coefficients; chain check |<v1 (x) v2|Psi_B> - P^B/Q^B <v2 (x) v2|Psi_B>|/|.| < 1e-147 on the six branches. Coefficients of the generic RREF representative (combination 1..6 of the reduced echelon basis; X^B itself is unique, only the normalisation of (P,Q) is conventional): eps-exponents of all 48 coefficients between eps = 1,2,4e-6 are in (-4e-4, +4e-3), i.e. all coefficients are O(1) with no poles in eps in this normalisation (first six are the identically constant pivots); the cancellation shows up instead in Q^B: min over the six branches |Q^B| = 3.5e-11, 1.39e-10, 5.56e-10 at eps = 1,2,4e-6, i.e. scaling as eps^2.",
   "languageId": "markdown",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 1,
   "value": "### gl(3) adj⊗adj localising-span result, final (2026-10-10, round 2 added)\n\n**Round 1 (above, cell 27)** stands: D2 rank 24 (4 relations), cubic 48, quartic 64; l1 = l2 = 3 with L1 = span{Om1, Om1 T11, Om1 T21}; polynomial torus, resolvent, second vacuum not in L1; Om1 rho(1/z) = -(128/75) Om1 T21 is.\n\n**Round 2, Task 5 (rational Q-numbers P/Q, exact, P1 and P1' identical).** Solution-space dimensions for Phi_v . Q = <Om (x) Om|P, per slot pair (P,Q) = (D1,D1),(D1,D2),(D2,D1),(D2,D2) (independent bases of size 7 and 24):\n\n| target | (D1,D1) | (D1,D2) | (D2,D1) | (D2,D2) |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| (a) polynomial torus, w2' = 3/7, -11/5, 9/4 | 0 | 0 | 0 | 0 |\n| (c) resolvent, two w2' | 0 | 0 | 0 | 0 |\n| (d) Om_w' (w' = (7/4,-2/5,9/7)) | 0 | 0 | 0 | 0 |\n| (d) Om_{(w1,y,1)}, y = 3, -1/2 | 0 | 0 | 0 | **6** |\n| (f) site 2: Om1 (x) (Om1 + kappa om2), kappa = 1, -2 | 0 | 0 | 0 | **5** |\n| (f) site 1: (Om1 + kappa om2) (x) Om1, kappa = 1, -2 | 0 | 0 | 0 | **6** |\n| (g) Om1 rho(1/z) control | 1 | 4 | 4 | 11 |\n| (g) random rational 8-vector | 0 | 0 | 0 | 0 |\n\nNo P = 0 solutions anywhere. For every solved target the representative has 24 nonzero c in P and 24 in Q, det Q (exact 64x64) != 0, Q^B != 0 on all 21 HW-sector states (min |Q^B| 1.38 (d), 67.6 (f) site 2 at P1), and the chain identity <v (x) Om1|Psi_B> Q^B = P^B <Om (x) Om|Psi_B> holds to < 1e-192 on all 21 states; X^B = P^B/Q^B is the same function on the whole solution space (rank 1).\n\n**Round 2, Task 3 for family (d)** (v2 = Om_w, v1 = Om_{(w1,y,1)}, y = 1+eps*eta): the undone covector phi_u has only TWO nonzero site-1 weights, (2,1,0) and (2,0,1), exactly and for all eps (the (1,2) entry of n(y) n(w2)^-1 is r1 - r1 = 0: the E12 direction is untouched because both vacua share w1). Hence: [4,2,0]: S ~ eps^-2, K = 0; [4,1,1]: S ~ eps^-3, K ~ eps^-2, max |K/S| = 1.11e-6, 2.22e-6, 4.43e-6 at eps = 1,2,4e-6 (phi) and 7.3e-7, 1.46e-6, 2.9e-6 (phi'), CG from overlap alone has the same linear-in-eps error and Richardson limit 46.67453891138 (phi) equal to the chain value (reference 46.67453891); [3,3,0], both octets and the singlet: S = 0 exactly, R_C = K (K ~ eps^-2, -3, -3, -4): no CG data, no octet mixing. (iv): exact (P,Q) at the regime point has dim 6, coefficients O(1) (no poles), chain deviation < 1e-147, Q^B ~ eps^2 minimum.\n\n**Structural conclusions.** (1) Rational P/Q of degree (2,2) exists for the same-w1 second vacuum and for the omega2 lines, not for (a), (c) or the different-w1 vacuum; (2) all solvable targets share w1 with the base vacuum and are rotations in the E13/E23 directions only, so their undone covectors miss the E12 direction (weights (1,2,0),(1,1,1),(1,0,2),(0,2,1),(0,1,2) vanish); the family untwists cleanly but is blind to four of the six HW branches. The gl(4)-like second deformation would need a w1-varying vacuum, which is not in the (2,2) rational span.",
   "languageId": "markdown",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 1,
   "value": "## Task 6. (P,Q) scan with two-site targets (round 3, Addendum B)\n\nBase vacuum Om_w (w = (w1,w2,.)), y* = y0 w2. T1: Phi = Om_{(w1,y1)} rho(1/(w2-z)) (x) Om_{(w1,y*)}; T2: Phi = Om_{(w1,y1)} rho(1/(w2'-z)) (x) Om_{(w1,y2)}; T3: T1 with the polynomial torus rho(w2-z); T4: y1 = y2 = 3. Controls: y1 = y* (the round-1 product point) and a random covector.",
   "languageId": "markdown",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 2,
   "value": "tg6[zz_, ww_] := Module[{w1 = ww[[1]], w2 = ww[[2]], ys, vac, T, out = {}},\n  ys = y0 w2; vac[y_] := oneSiteVac[zz, {w1, y, 1}];\n  T[y1_, y2_, wp_, kind_] := Flatten[Outer[Times, vac[y1] . ρdiag[If[kind === \"res\", 1/(wp - zz), wp - zz]], vac[y2]]];\n  Join[\n   Table[\"T1 y1=\" <> ToString[y] -> T[y, ys, w2, \"res\"], {y, {3, -1/2, 7/5}}],\n   {\"control y1=y* (product point)\" -> T[ys, ys, w2, \"res\"]},\n   {\"T2 (y1,y2,w2')=(3,y*,9/4)\" -> T[3, ys, 9/4, \"res\"], \"T2 (3,2,w2)\" -> T[3, 2, w2, \"res\"], \"T2 (3,y*(9/4),9/4)\" -> T[3, y0 9/4, 9/4, \"res\"]},\n   Table[\"T3 poly torus y1=\" <> ToString[y] -> T[y, ys, w2, \"poly\"], {y, {3, -1/2, 7/5}}],\n   {\"T4 y1=y2=3\" -> T[3, 3, w2, \"res\"]},\n   {\"random covector\" -> (SeedRandom[11]; Table[RandomInteger[{-5, 5}]/RandomInteger[{1, 5}], {64}])}]];\ntask6table[zz_, ww_] := Module[{tc = tZexact[zz], om = oneSiteVac[zz, ww], Om2, tg = tg6[zz, ww]},\n  Om2 = Flatten[KroneckerProduct[om, om]];\n  Table[t[[1]] -> Table[With[{r = t5solve[Om2, t[[2]], basisOf[tc, pq[[1]]], basisOf[tc, pq[[2]]]]}, {r[\"dim\"], r[\"dimQ0\"]}], {pq, {{1, 1}, {1, 2}, {2, 1}, {2, 2}}}], {t, tg}]];\n{tT6, t6P1} = AbsoluteTiming[task6table[zP1, wP1]];\nt6P1c = task6table[zP1c, wP1c];\nGrid[Join[{{\"time P1 (s)\", tT6}, {\"entries {dim, dim(P=0)} for (P,Q) = (D1,D1),(D1,D2),(D2,D1),(D2,D2)\", \"\"}, {\"P1\", \"\"}}, Table[{t[[1]], ToString[t[[2]]]}, {t, t6P1}], {{\"P1'\", \"\"}}, Table[{t[[1]], ToString[t[[2]]]}, {t, t6P1c}]], Frame -> All, Alignment -> Left]",
   "languageId": "wolfram",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 1,
   "value": "**Task 6 result (cell 45, 9.5 s, P1 and P1' identical).** Entries {dim, dim with P=0} for (P,Q) = (D1,D1),(D1,D2),(D2,D1),(D2,D2).\n\n- **T1** (y1 = 3, -1/2, 7/5; Om_{(w1,y1)} rho(1/(w2-z)) (x) Om_{(w1,y*)}): dimension 0 in all four pairs, at both points. **T1 does not solve.**\n- Control y1 = y* (the round-1 product point): dimensions 0, 0, 3, 5 for (D1,D1),(D1,D2),(D2,D1),(D2,D2): solves with Q constant allowed (D2,D1), consistent with round 1.\n- T2 (3,y*,9/4), (3,2,w2), (3,y*(9/4),9/4): 0 in all pairs. T3 (polynomial torus, y1 = 3, -1/2, 7/5): 0. T4 (y1 = y2 = 3): 0. Random 64-covector: 0.\n- No representative or chain check is needed (nothing solved except the control, already verified in round 1 as an element of the image of D2).\n\nBy the spec's rule Task 7 (untwist) is conditional on T1 solving: not run. Below, a short exploratory scan of which two-site targets of this shape do solve.",
   "languageId": "markdown",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
