   "kind": 1,
   "value": "## Task 7 (not run) and Task 8\n\n**Task 7** is conditional on T1 solving; T1 has solution dimension 0 in all four slot pairs for y1 = 3, -1/2, 7/5 at both P1 and P1' (and T2, T3, T4 and the random covector also 0), so no untwist run was done and there are no Task-7 tables.\n\n**Task 8 (cost).** For the targets that DO solve (two common-w1 vacua with free y's; the round-2 families) the Q-number needs the six eigenvalue coefficients alpha = (t1^(0), t1^(1), t2^(0..3)) (t1 at 2 points, t2 at 4), det6(w), and one rational function P^B/Q^B of degree (2,2) in alpha: 24 + 24 coefficients (48 nonzero for a generic representative), independent of the representation at L = 2. The product point with the resolvent factor is a polynomial of degree 2 (round 1 (e): 18 nonzero coefficients) and the y1-deformed version of it is NOT in the (2,2) rational span.",
