  {
   "kind": 1,
   "value": "### gl(3) adj⊗adj localising-span result, final (2026-10-10, round 3 added)\n\nRounds 1 and 2: see cells 27 and 43 (D2 rank 24, cubic 48, quartic 64; l1 = 3; (2,2) rational forms for Om_{(w1,y)} families; the y-family untwists but sees only [4,2,0] and [4,1,1], Richardson limit 46.67453891138 for [4,1,1]).\n\n**Round 3, Task 6.** Target Phi = Om_{(w1,y1)} rho(1/(w2-z)) (x) Om_{(w1,y*)} (y* = y0 w2 = -63/8 at P1, 27/20 at P1'), y1 = 3, -1/2, 7/5: solution dimension **0** in (D1,D1), (D1,D2), (D2,D1), (D2,D2), at P1 and P1'. Control y1 = y* solves: dims (0,0,3,5), i.e. Q constant allowed. T2 (three variants), T3 (polynomial torus, three y1), T4 (y1 = y2 = 3), random covector: all 0. Task 7 not run (T1 does not solve).\n\n**Exploratory, round 3.** Common-w1 vacuum products Om_{(w1,y1)} (x) Om_{(w1,y2)} solve in (D2,D2) (dim 4; 4 with y2 = y*; 6 with base on site 2; 5 reversed) but any target with a torus factor rho(1/(w'-z)) or rho(1/z) on a y-deformed vacuum does not (0), including the symmetric and mixed variants. So the E12/E13 localising torus and the y1 deformation do not combine inside D2/D2 rational forms; the undone covector of the solvable products is blind to the E12 direction (round 2). Whether the composite lies in a larger rational span (degrees (2,3), (3,3), or D2/D2 with an inserted second ratio) is not tested.",
   "languageId": "markdown",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
