   "kind": 2,
   "value": "pivD3[tc_] := indepPiv[d3Basis][tc];\nbasis3[tc_] := d3Basis[tc][[pivD3[tc]]];\nev3[al_] := Join[evOf[al], Flatten[Table[al[[i]] al[[j]] al[[k]], {i, 6}, {j, i, 6}, {k, j, 6}]]];\n(* selection by position, not by string key: keys with rational arguments contain 2D-formatted strings *)\ntargets9[zz_, ww_] := Module[{tg = tgts[zz, ww], t6 = tg6[zz, ww], pick},\n  pick[l_, s_] := Select[l, StringStartsQ[#[[1]], s] &];\n  Join[pick[tg, \"(a)\"], pick[tg, \"(c)\"], {\"T1 y1=3\" -> pick[t6, \"T1\"][[1, 2]], \"T1 y1=-1/2\" -> pick[t6, \"T1\"][[2, 2]], \"T1 y1=7/5\" -> pick[t6, \"T1\"][[3, 2]]}, pick[tg, \"(d) Om_w'\"], {\"ctl product point\" -> pick[t6, \"control\"][[1, 2]], \"ctl Om_(w1,3) (x) Om1\" -> pick[tg, \"(d) y=3\"][[1, 2]], \"ctl Om1 rho(1/z)\" -> pick[tg, \"(g) Om1 rho\"][[1, 2]], \"ctl random covector\" -> pick[t6, \"random\"][[1, 2]]}]];\ntask9table[zz_, ww_] := Module[{tc = tZexact[zz], om = oneSiteVac[zz, ww], Om2, B3, B1, tg},\n  Om2 = Flatten[KroneckerProduct[om, om]]; B3 = basis3[tc]; B1 = d1Basis[tc];\n  tg = targets9[zz, ww];\n  Table[t[[1]] -> {t5solve[Om2, t[[2]], B3, {id2}][\"dim\"], t5solve[Om2, t[[2]], B3, B1][\"dim\"]}, {t, tg}]];\n{tT9, t9P1} = AbsoluteTiming[task9table[zP1, wP1]];\nt9P1c = task9table[zP1c, wP1c];\nGrid[Join[{{\"time P1 (s)\", tT9}, {\"rank D3 independent basis size\", Length[basis3[tZexact[zP1]]]}, {\"entries {dim (D3,1), dim (D3,D1)}; P1\", \"\"}}, Table[{ToString[t[[1]]], ToString[t[[2]]]}, {t, t9P1}], {{\"P1'\", \"\"}}, Table[{ToString[t[[1]]], ToString[t[[2]]]}, {t, t9P1c}]], Frame -> All, Alignment -> Left]",
   "languageId": "wolfram",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 1,
   "value": "**Task 9 result (cell 52, 2.3 s per point, P1 and P1' identical; the first draft keyed T1 y1 = -1/2 by a 2D-formatted string and returned a spurious dim 1, fixed by selecting by position).** Independent cubic basis: 48 operators. Entries {dim (D3,1), dim (D3,D1)}:\n\n- (a) w2' = 3/7, -11/5, 9/4 (13/10 not used): {0,0}, {0,0}, {0,0}. (c) two w2': {0,0}. T1 y1 = 3, -1/2, 7/5: {0,0} each. (d) Om_{w'} (different w1): {0,0}. Random covector: {0,0}.\n- Controls: product point {1, 7} (polynomial, unique P with Q = 1; in (D3,D1) the 7 solutions are Q in D1 times the same X); Om1 rho(1/z) (x) Om1 {1, 7}; Om_{(w1,3)} (x) Om1 {0,0}: the (2,2)-rational y-family is not in (D3,D1).\n\nSo nothing new is reachable at (D3,D1): no representative, sparse denominator or chain check applies.",
   "languageId": "markdown",
