  {
   "kind": 1,
   "value": "**Task 10 (iv) result (cells 59, 60; 0.06 s and 0.1 s; P1 and P1' identical).** Site-2 column space of <Om Om|X over the 8-operator family {1, T10, T11, T20, T21 at th1-2h, t2(th1), t2(th2+h), t2(th2+h)t1(th2-h)}: **dimension 5** (as expected), containing Om1 and omega2; 3 directions beyond the E23 line span{Om1, omega2}. Per operator (rank of Phi_X, dim of its site-2 rows modulo the line): 1: (1,0); T10: (2,0); T11: (1,0); T20: (2,0); T21: (1,0): all inside the line. t2(th1): (2,1) with 2 basis rows, of which one is a rotation and one is not, and it adds exactly one new direction; t2(th2+h): (1,1) not a rotation; t2(th2+h)t1(th2-h): (1,1) not a rotation. The t2(th2+h) and B2 directions are not proportional; the rank of all directions together with Om1, omega2 is 5, of the two rank-1 directions with the line 4, of t2(th1) with the line 3. So the three new directions are NOT common-w1 vacua: the localising operators T10, T11, T20, T21 stay on the E23 line, and the operators outside the theta1-2h family (t2(th1), t2(th2+h), B2) bring in three directions that are (mostly) not rotations.",
   "languageId": "markdown",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
