  {
   "kind": 1,
   "value": "### gl(3) adj⊗adj localising-span result, final (2026-10-10, round 4: complete reachability map)\n\n**Algebra.** D1 rank 7, D2 rank 24 (4 quadratic relations among the six a_i), D3 rank 48, D4 rank 64 (all End; vacuous).\n\n**Site-1 covectors (times the vacuum Om1 on site 2) reachable at each level (P1 and P1' identical):**\n\n| level | reachable | not reachable (all dims 0) |\n|---|---|---|\n| polynomial D1 | span{Om1, Om1 T11} (l1 = 2) | |\n| polynomial D2 (l1 = 3) and D3 (l1 = 3) | L1 = span{Om1, Om1 T11^(1), Om1 T21^(1)}; contains exactly the tori d = 1 and d = 1/z (Om1 rho(1/z) = -(128/75) Om1 T21 at P1) | polynomial torus Om1 rho(w2'-z), Om1 rho(z), resolvent, second vacua |\n| rational (D2,D2) | Om_{(w1,y)} (6), omega2 lines (5, 6), products of two common-w1 vacua (4 to 6); the product point (polynomial, 18 nonzero c) | polynomial torus (a), resolvent (c), different-w1 vacuum Om_{w'}, every torus-times-y-deformed-vacuum target T1..T4 |\n| rational (D3,1), (D3,D1) | only controls (product point, Om1 rho(1/z): dims 1 and 7) | (a), (c), T1 (y1 = 3, -1/2, 7/5), Om_{w'}, and even Om_{(w1,3)} (x) Om1 |\n| rational (D2,D1), (D1,D2), (D1,D1) | Om1 rho(1/z) only | everything else tried |\n| D4 / (D3,D2) | vacuous by counting | |\n\n**Torus content of the localising span.** T21^(1) at th1-2h is diagonal: -(3/8) prod z_k^(2-mu_k) = -3 h^3 chi3^2 prod z^-mu on every weight, i.e. exactly the inverse torus rho(1/z) times a scalar. T11^(1) is not a torus: it is diagonal on the six 1-dim weights with eigenvalue (3/4) chi3/z_m (m = index with mu_m = 2) but has an off-diagonal, non-scalar block on (1,1,1) with eigenvalues (e2 -/+ sqrt(e2^2 - 3 e1 e3))/4; it matches none of the candidates (e1(1/z), rho(1/z) e1(z), e2 of {z^mu}, e1/e2 of the complementary multiset). Exact solve Om1(c0 + k1 T11 + k2 T21) = Om1 rho(d): only {0, d = 1, d = 1/z}; the same for the 5-dim span including T10, T20 in sum-of-products form with the corrected second rotation omega2 = Om1 rho(exp(gamma(E23 - a E13))) (gamma = -65/44, a = 4/5 at P1; the spec's pure E23 form is false). The 8-dim enlarged family has a 5-dim site-2 column space = E23 line (2) + 3 non-vacuum directions from t2(th1), t2(th2+h), t2(th2+h)t1(th2-h); the localising operators T10..T21 stay on the line.\n\n**Conclusion.** No free-parameter torus (no kappa-family analogue) exists in any of the structured spans D1, D2, D3, (2,2) and (3,1) rational: the only torus translates are 1 and 1/z. A polynomial-torus Q-number of the gl(4) type would need a different source (degree-4 polynomials in the six a_i are vacuous; or an inverse-transfer-matrix form as at L = 1 with larger degree). Task 11 (untwist of a free-torus family) was therefore not run.\n\nSee also rounds 1-3 above (cells 27, 43, 50) for the D2 localising spaces, the (2,2) y-family untwist (reads only [4,2,0], [4,1,1]) and the failed torus-times-y composite.",
   "languageId": "markdown",
   "outputs": [],
